:: Lost Lamb Main Widgets [widget]
<<widget 'lost-lamb-main'>>
  <<switch $LostLamb.scene>>
    <<case 'main-start'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You put out two cups without being told. The handles face the same way. You lift the book off the drawing and lay out the pencils, including the short one Sydney always chooses after saying it is useless.
          <br><br>
          The clock strikes. You carry a chair to the window, then stand on the floor again because Sydney will laugh if <<nnpc_he 'Sydney'>> catches you watching. Nobody knocks.
          <br><br>
          Your parent comes through with a basket of washing. "What are you doing there?"
          <br><br>
          You point to the cups. The basket is set down before they answer. "Sydney isn't coming today."
          <br><br>
          You ask about tomorrow. Your parent looks towards the laboratory, then picks the basket up again. "We'll have to see."
          <br><br>
          Outside, a shop delivery goes past the gate. You watch it until it has gone. Inside, the square of sunlight still reaches almost to the stairs. You glance at the clock. Its hands have moved much farther than the light.
          <br><br>
          You shift Sydney's cup closer to your own so nobody will mistake it for one that needs putting away.
          <br><br>
          You leave room for Sydney's bag beside the things you meant to show. One more minute. You go back to the window. By the time you turn round, the sunlight has moved off the empty place.
          <br><br>
          There are people in the street. None is coming through the gate yet. You leave the window to look from closer by.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          不用人提醒，你就摆出两个杯子，杯柄转向同一侧。你挪开压着画纸的书，摆出铅笔，包括悉尼每次都说没用了、却每次都选的那支短笔。
          <br><br>
          钟响了。你把椅子搬到窗边，又站回地上，免得悉尼发现你在盯着外面，拿这件事笑你。没人敲门。
          <br><br>
          父母抱着装衣服的篮子经过。“在那里做什么？”
          <br><br>
          你指指杯子。篮子先被放下，对方才回答。“悉尼今天不来。”
          <br><br>
          你问明天呢。父母看向实验室，又把篮子抱起来。“到时候再说。”
          <br><br>
          商店送货的车经过门外。你一直看到它不见。屋里，那块方形的日光仍然差一点就碰到楼梯。你看看钟。指针走得比光远多了。
          <br><br>
          你把悉尼的杯子挪得离自己的更近些，免得有人以为那是需要收起来的。
          <br><br>
          你把本来想给悉尼看的东西摆好，旁边留着放包的位置。再等一分钟。你回到窗前，再转过身时，日光已经离开了那块空地。
          <br><br>
          街上有人来来往往，却还没有一个走进大门。隔着窗户，你始终看不清他们会不会在路口转过来。你离开窗边，想再走近一些，从门口看。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-missed'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          Your parent answers the first question while putting things away. At the second, the cupboard stays open. At the third, a cup lands hard enough to click against the one beside it.
          <br><br>
          "Sydney can't visit. Sydney's family has said so."
          <br><br>
          "For how long?"
          <br><br>
          "Kylar."
          <br><br>
          You wait. Your parent closes the cupboard and turns to you. Their face looks tired. They reach to smooth your hair, but you duck beneath the hand and ask whether you did something wrong.
          <br><br>
          "No." This answer comes at once. The hand stops in the air, then rests on your shoulder instead. "You haven't done anything."
          <br><br>
          You ask if they can go and talk to Sydney's parent. Your parent squeezes your shoulder, harder than before. "You mustn't go over there yourself. Do you understand?"
          <br><br>
          From the laboratory, your other parent calls. The hand leaves you. A key is taken from the table and slipped into a pocket. You hear it turn in the lock after your parent has gone inside. You stand by the cupboard with your next question ready.
          <br><br>
          Later you stand where the two coats used to touch. Yours is on the hook. Sydney's is not. You press the empty sleeve of your own coat against your cheek, feeling the cold wool, then stop when you hear a parent coming.
          <br><br>
          They said you mustn't go to Sydney's house. They didn't say you couldn't wait at the school gate. You remember which one Sydney uses.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          父母一边收东西，一边回答第一个问题。问第二个时，柜门一直没关。问到第三个，杯子放得太重，和旁边的那只磕出一声脆响。
          <br><br>
          “悉尼不能来。<<nnpc_his 'Sydney'>>家里这么说了。”
          <br><br>
          “要多久？”
          <br><br>
          “凯拉尔。”
          <br><br>
          你等着。父母关上柜门，转向你，脸上很疲倦。对方想替你抚平头发，你从手底下躲开，问是不是自己做错了什么。
          <br><br>
          “不是。”这次立刻得到回答。那只手停在半空，改落到肩上。“你没做错什么。”
          <br><br>
          你问，能不能去找悉尼的家长说说。肩膀被捏了一下，比刚才重。“你不能自己跑去那里。明白吗？”
          <br><br>
          实验室里，另一位父母喊了一声。肩上的手离开了。桌上的钥匙被拿起，塞进口袋。父母进门后，你听见钥匙在锁里转动。你站在柜子旁，下一句要问的话还在嘴边。
          <br><br>
          后来，你站在两件外套以前会碰到一起的位置。自己的外套仍挂在钩子上，悉尼的那件却不在。你把自己空着的袖子贴在脸颊上，感觉羊毛冷冷的。听见父母靠近的脚步，你赶紧放下，不想让对方看见自己这样。
          <br><br>
          他们说不能去悉尼家，可没说不能在学校门口等。你还记得，悉尼放学会从哪扇门出来。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-school'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You find Sydney near the yard gate as everyone begins to leave. A bag knocks against somebody's knees. Children hurry past you, shouting things you cannot follow. One has a sleeve turned inside out and is being called back to fix it.
          <br><br>
          Sydney sees you and slows. You almost lift both hands, the way you did from the bedroom window. <<nnpc_He 'Sydney'>> looks behind <<nnpc_himself 'Sydney'>> instead. An adult is waiting beyond the gate.
          <br><br>
          You say <<nnpc_his 'Sydney'>> name louder than you meant to. Sydney comes close before you can call again. There is still a little pencil lead on <<nnpc_his 'Sydney'>> thumb. You want to point it out. You want to tell <<nnpc_him 'Sydney'>> how many afternoons you waited.
          <br><br>
          "I can't come over," <<nnpc_he 'Sydney'>> says.
          <br><br>
          "You haven't come for ages."
          <br><br>
          Sydney's face changes. You meant the words to make <<nnpc_him 'Sydney'>> understand, but <<nnpc_he 'Sydney'>> lowers <<nnpc_his 'Sydney'>> eyes as though you have said something in front of everyone. You step away from the gate so the others can pass. The bell is still sounding behind you, far longer than it usually does.
          <br><br>
          You talk faster. The game, the thing on your shelf, the short pencil you put aside. Sydney glances towards the gate. You move in front of <<nnpc_him 'Sydney'>>. When <<nnpc_he 'Sydney'>> tries the other side, you step there too.
          <br><br>
          Someone outside calls Sydney's name. <<nnpc_He 'Sydney'>> jumps. You jump too, then pretend you have only moved to let another child through. Your hand is level with Sydney's sleeve. You curl it into a fist before anyone sees.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你在院子大门附近找到悉尼，大家正开始离开。有人走动，书包撞着膝盖。孩子们从身边匆匆经过，喊着你没听明白的话。一个人的袖子翻了出来，被叫回去整理。
          <br><br>
          悉尼看见你，脚步慢了。你差点像在卧室窗前那样，两只手都抬起来。<<nnpc_He 'Sydney'>>却先往身后看。大门外有个大人在等。
          <br><br>
          你喊出<<nnpc_his 'Sydney'>>的名字，比自己想的响。没等再喊，悉尼就走近了。悉尼的拇指上还留着一点铅笔灰。你想指出来，也想告诉<<nnpc_him 'Sydney'>>，自己等了多少个下午。
          <br><br>
          “我不能去你家。”<<nnpc_He 'Sydney'>>说。
          <br><br>
          “你已经好久没来了。”
          <br><br>
          悉尼的表情变了。你想让<<nnpc_he 'Sydney'>>明白，可<<nnpc_he 'Sydney'>>垂下眼，像你当着所有人的面说了什么。你挪到门旁，让别人过去。身后的铃还在响，比平时长得多。
          <br><br>
          你越说越快。那个游戏，架子上的东西，专门留好的短铅笔。悉尼往大门看，你便挡到<<nnpc_him 'Sydney'>>前面。<<nnpc_He 'Sydney'>>想从另一边走，你也迈过去。
          <br><br>
          外面有人喊悉尼的名字。<<nnpc_He 'Sydney'>>吓得一抖，你也抖了一下，随后假装自己只是要让别的孩子经过。你的手与悉尼的袖子一样高。赶在有人看见以前，你把它握成了拳头。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-return'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('drawing-carried')>>You unfold the drawing. Sydney touches the pencilled window with one finger. "I remember." You ask why <<nnpc_he 'Sydney'>> cannot finish it. <<nnpc_He 'Sydney'>> takes the finger away, leaving the window just as it was. You hold the paper closer so <<nnpc_he 'Sydney'>> can see the door too.<<else>>You ask why the visits stopped. Sydney opens <<nnpc_his 'Sydney'>> mouth, stops, then tries again. You wait. If you speak now, <<nnpc_he 'Sydney'>> might answer the easier question instead.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          "I'm not allowed. They said..."
          <br><br>
          The bell covers the next few words. You lean closer. It stops at last. Sydney has stopped too. <<nnpc_He 'Sydney'>> looks at the adult beyond the gate, whose face you cannot see past the other people.
          <br><br>
          "Ask again," you say.
          <br><br>
          "I did."
          <br><br>
          You begin to tell Sydney that <<nnpc_he 'Sydney'>> could come without asking. Then you remember your own parent's hand on your shoulder. Sydney steps backwards before you can finish.
          <br><br>
          Someone calls <<nnpc_his 'Sydney'>> name. <<nnpc_He 'Sydney'>> says goodbye, quietly, and walks through the gate. The adult takes the bag. You watch until a cart crosses in front of them. When it has passed, you cannot find the two figures among the others. Your hand is still raised with nothing in it.
          <br><br>
          You leave without saying the sentence you practised. On the pavement you try it under your breath. The question sounds like a complaint now, so you stop before the end.
          <br><br>
          The woman outside the shop is putting bread in a bag. You know the brown paper your parents bring home. A child waits beside her, eating a piece before the rest has been wrapped. You slow down to watch, then hurry when the woman looks at you.
          <br><br>
          You could go straight home. You could take the lane past the other shops and make your parents wait for a change. You imagine somebody coming to the gate to look for you. Then you imagine having to say where you have been.
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('drawing-carried')>>The drawing rubs against your sleeve. A corner has bent. You smooth it on your leg as you walk, but it turns up again at once.<<else>>You look at your empty hand. You could have brought the drawing. Sydney might have stayed to look at it. You curl your fingers into your palm and walk on.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          At the junction, you can see the manor roof between two houses. You turn your head towards the other road. The roof is there too, farther off, though that road should lead away from home. A cart goes by. You wait for it to pass and look again. Whichever road you take, you can still see one bright upstairs window.
          <br><br>
          At home your parent asks about your day. You say it was fine before remembering that it was not. The question has already moved on to supper. You sit down and find that being angry does not stop you being hungry.
          <br><br>
          For several days you eat at the same table and hang your coat on the same hook. Sydney's chair stays empty. Your button works loose, and you keep forgetting to ask about it.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('drawing-carried')>>你展开画纸。悉尼用一根手指碰了碰铅笔画的窗。“我记得。”你问为什么不能把它画完。<<nnpc_He 'Sydney'>>把手指收走，窗还是原来的样子。你将纸拿近些，让<<nnpc_he 'Sydney'>>也看看那扇门。<<else>>你问为什么不再来了。悉尼张口，停住，又重新试了一遍。你等着。如果现在插话，<<nnpc_he 'Sydney'>>也许就会挑容易的那个问题回答。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          “不让我去。我的另一位家长说……”
          <br><br>
          后面几句话被铃声盖住。你靠近些。铃终于停了，悉尼也停了。<<nnpc_He 'Sydney'>>看向门外的大人，人群挡着，你看不清那人的脸。
          <br><br>
          “再问一次。”你说。
          <br><br>
          “我问过。”
          <br><br>
          你开始说，不用问也能来。随后想起自己肩上那只父母的手。没说完，悉尼已经往后退了一步。
          <br><br>
          有人喊<<nnpc_his 'Sydney'>>的名字。<<nnpc_He 'Sydney'>>轻轻说了再见，穿过大门，大人接过书包。你一直看着，一辆车从两人前面驶过。车走了，你却在其他人中找不到那两道身影了。手还抬着，里面什么也没有。
          <br><br>
          你没说出练习过的那句话就走了。在人行道上，又低声试一遍。问题现在听着像抱怨，你没说到最后就停下。
          <br><br>
          商店门外，一个女人正把面包装进袋子。那种牛皮纸你认得，父母也会拎回家。旁边的孩子等着，面包还没包好，就已经拿了一片吃。你慢下来，看了看。女人抬眼时，你又赶紧走快。
          <br><br>
          可以直接回家，也可以沿另一条巷子经过更多商店，让父母也等一回。你想象有人到门边找自己。接着，又想到得解释去了哪里。
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('drawing-carried')>>画纸擦着袖子，一角弯了。你边走边在腿上把它抹平，它却立刻又翘起来。<<else>>你看看空着的手。本来可以带画来的，悉尼也许会为看它多留一会儿。你把手指蜷进掌心，继续走。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          岔路口，两座房子中间露出庄园的屋顶。你转头看向另一条路，屋顶在那里也能看见，更远些，尽管那条路应该离家越来越远。一辆车驶过。你等它过去，又看了一次。不管选哪条路，都看得见楼上那一扇明亮的窗。
          <br><br>
          回到家时，父母问起你今天过得怎样。你先说了很好，随后才想起来，其实并不好。可话题已经转到了晚饭。你坐到桌旁，这才发现，即使生气，肚子也还是会饿。
          <br><br>
          接下来几天，你照常在桌边吃饭，把外套挂回原来的钩子。悉尼的椅子一直空着。你的扣子越来越松，却总忘了让父母看看。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-small-help'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          A button comes off your coat while you are trying to hang it up. You hear it hit the floor and put a shoe over it before it can roll beneath the cupboard. For a moment you are pleased with yourself. Then you remember that the button should not have come off at all.
          <br><br>
          Your parent finds you holding it. You explain too quickly: you were not pulling, it was already loose, you had only been putting the coat away. The explanation grows longer than anything that happened. Your parent holds out a hand.
          <br><br>
          "The coat as well, Kylar. I can't sew it onto your hand."
          <br><br>
          You give both things over. They fetch the little box and sit in the good light. You remain standing until they tap the place beside them. You sit without saying that you had wanted to be asked.
          <br><br>
          The thread will not go through the needle. Your parent tries twice, complains, then puts the needle in your hand. You get it through on the first try and wish somebody else had seen. Your parent says not to look so pleased. They are smiling while they say it.
          <br><br>
          You watch the button turn with each stitch. You ask why the thread is doubled. Your parent folds it over your finger to show you. You ask whether Sydney would be good at this. "Bring <<nnpc_him 'Sydney'>> a needle next time and find out." Then the hand stops. Your parent pulls the thread tight and looks at the knot instead of you.
          <br><br>
          "Could you talk to Sydney's..." Your parent lays the coat across your knees and gives the button a gentle tug. You look down at it, leaving the question unfinished.
          <br><br>
          "There. Don't pull it off to check my work."
          <br><br>
          You nearly pull it. They catch your wrist before you can and laugh. You put the coat on and try the button once. It holds. You go back to the hall, rubbing your thumb over the new stitches.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你想把外套挂好时，一颗扣子掉了下来。你听见它碰到地板，赶在它滚进柜子底下之前，用鞋盖住了它。有那么一瞬间，你为自己反应这么快有些得意。随后才想起来，扣子本来就不该掉。
          <br><br>
          父母中的一人发现了你，你正把扣子捏在手里。你急急忙忙解释：自己没有拉它，它本来就松了，你只是想把外套放好。解释说得比刚才发生过的全部事情还长。对方朝你伸出了手。
          <br><br>
          “外套也给我，凯拉尔。我总不能把它缝在你手上。”
          <br><br>
          你把两样东西都递过去。对方取来装针线的小盒子，坐到光线好的地方。你一直站在旁边，直到对方拍拍身侧的位置，你才坐下。你没有说，其实自己一直想被这样叫过去。
          <br><br>
          线怎么也穿不过针眼。对方试了两次，抱怨了一句，随后把针放进你手里。你第一次就穿了过去，恨不得有别人在这里也能看见。对方说，别那么得意。说这句话的时候，脸上却带着笑。
          <br><br>
          你看着扣子随每一针慢慢转动。你问为什么要把线折成两股，父母就在你的手指上折一次，让你看。你问悉尼会不会也做得很好。“下次给<<nnpc_him 'Sydney'>>一根针，试试就知道。”随后，那只手停住。父母拉紧线，盯着线结，没有看你。
          <br><br>
          “能不能找悉尼家里……”父母把外套放在你膝上，轻轻拉了拉扣子。你低头看着它，没有把问题问完。
          <br><br>
          “好了。别为了检查我缝得好不好，又把它扯掉。”
          <br><br>
          你差点真去拉它。对方先捉住手腕，笑了起来。你穿上外套，试着扣了一次，扣子没有松。回到大厅时，你还用拇指摸着新缝的线。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-evening'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          Your parents are excited. They keep interrupting each other, then laughing as though the interruptions are part of a joke you have missed. One of them has already set out a clean cup without putting anything in it.
          <br><br>
          You scrape the last food from your plate. Nobody tells you to stop making that noise. Both heads turn towards the hall instead. You turn too, expecting someone in the doorway. There is only the coat hanging from its hook.
          <br><br>
          "Who's coming?"
          <br><br>
          Your parent looks back at you. The smile stays, but the answer does not arrive. "Bedtime."
          <br><br>
          You point at the window. It is not dark yet. Usually this would be enough to earn you another few minutes. Tonight your parent takes your plate while you are still holding the spoon. The spoon knocks against the table.
          <br><br>
          "Early tonight."
          <br><br>
          You tuck your feet under the chair. Perhaps there is a present. Perhaps they need you out of the way to carry it in. You try to hear whether anything is waiting outside, but your parents have begun talking again. One puts a hand on the back of your chair. You know you have to get up.
          <br><br>
          Before you leave the table, you ask whether the cup is for Sydney's parent. Both adults hear the name. One shakes their head; the other puts the cup farther from your elbow. Nobody says Sydney is coming.
          <br><br>
          You look at the empty chair. A moment ago you were sure the evening was going to give something back. Now you do not know what the excitement is for, and the ordinary bedtime words have come too early.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          父母很兴奋。他们不断打断对方，然后笑起来，仿佛打断也是某个笑话的一部分，只有你没听懂。其中一人已经摆出一只干净杯子，里面却什么也没倒。
          <br><br>
          你用勺子刮盘里最后一点食物。没人让你别弄出这种声音。两个人都转头看向大厅。你也跟着转，以为门口会有人。那里只有挂在钩子上的外套。
          <br><br>
          “谁要来？”
          <br><br>
          父母转回来。笑容还在，却没有回答。“该睡觉了。”
          <br><br>
          你指指窗外。天还没黑。平时，这就足够换来几分钟。今晚，你还握着勺子，父母就拿走了盘子。勺子敲在桌上。
          <br><br>
          “今晚早点睡。”
          <br><br>
          你把脚缩到椅子下面。也许是礼物。也许搬进来时得先把你支开。你想听听外面是不是有什么在等，父母却又聊了起来。一只手搭上椅背。你知道该起身了。
          <br><br>
          离开餐桌以前，你忍不住问，那只杯子是不是给悉尼的家长准备的。两位父母都听见了那个名字。其中一人摇摇头，另一人把杯子挪得离你的手肘远些。没有人说，悉尼今晚会来。
          <br><br>
          你望着空椅子。片刻之前，你几乎确信，这个傍晚终于要把什么还给自己。现在，你不明白他们究竟在兴奋什么。那些再熟悉不过的睡觉前的话，也比平时来得早了太多。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-bed'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('eve-ask')>>You ask again on the stairs. "What are you happy about?" Your parent almost answers, then looks past you towards the landing. "Tomorrow." You ask whether that is a promise. This time the reply is your name, said sharply enough to make you stop.<<else>>You ask to stay up until the visitor arrives. Your parent says you will be tired tomorrow. You say you are not tired now. The hand at your back keeps you moving up the stairs while you explain.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          Your shirt is twisted at the neck. You pull it straight while your parent checks the window. The catch clicks. It is tried once more, harder. You have never noticed how small that piece of metal is.
          <br><br>
          The covers are smoothed over your knees. You ask for the usual gap in the door, enough to see the landing light. Your parent leaves it, then comes back and pulls the door almost shut. The bright strip becomes a thread. You wait for an explanation. Footsteps go downstairs instead.
          <br><br>
          You sit up to reach the handle, then hear a chair dragged below. You lie down before you have put your feet on the floor. If you open the door, they will know you are still awake. If you leave it alone, you cannot see who crosses the landing.
          <br><br>
          For an instant you remember another bedroom, and a way up to an attic. Neither is anywhere you can reach with your legs curled beneath these covers. You turn your pillow over to the cool side. The door remains shut. You are supposed to sleep, and there is nobody left here to ask how.
          <br><br>
          You put one shoe beside the other so you will not have to search in the morning. They look smaller side by side than they did on your feet.
          <br><br>
          You nearly call for your parent to come back. It would be an ordinary reason: the door, the light, a drink of water. You rehearse one of them beneath your breath. Downstairs somebody laughs, and you decide to wait until the laugh is finished.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('eve-ask')>>上楼时，你又问了一次。“你们为什么那么高兴？”父母差点回答，随后越过你看向楼梯间。“明天。”你问是不是答应了。这次对方只喊了你的名字，语气重得让你住了口。<<else>>你想等到来客到时再睡。父母说，明天会累。你说现在一点也不累。你解释着，背后的手却一直带你往楼上走。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          上衣在领口拧住了。你把它拉正，父母去检查窗户。搭扣咔哒一声，又被更用力地试了一次。你从没注意过，这一小块金属有多小。
          <br><br>
          被子在膝上抚平。你要门留下平时那条缝，够看见楼梯间的灯。父母留下了，又回来把门拉到几乎关紧。亮条变成一根线。你等着听解释，脚步却下楼去了。
          <br><br>
          你坐起来，想去够门把，楼下忽然拖动了一把椅子。脚还没落地，你便躺了回去。开门，他们就知道你没睡。不打开，就看不见谁经过楼梯间。
          <br><br>
          一瞬间，你想起另一间卧室，还有一条通往阁楼的路。双腿蜷在这床被子下面，哪里也走不到。你把枕头翻到凉的一面。门仍关着。你应该睡觉，这里却已经没有人能让你问该怎样睡。
          <br><br>
          你把两只鞋并排摆好，想着早晨就不用四处找。它们放在一起时，看起来比穿在脚上还要小。你看了好一会儿，才把脚收回床上。
          <br><br>
          你差一点叫父母回来。理由可以非常普通：门还没弄好，灯太亮，或者你想喝一杯水。你在嘴里小声练习其中一个理由。楼下忽然有人笑了起来，你又决定，先等那个笑声结束。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-noise'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          The crash throws you upright before you know you were asleep. Something small strikes the floor below, then many small things at once. Glass. You know that sound from the cup you once dropped, only this keeps going.
          <br><br>
          Another window breaks downstairs. The wall beside your bed gives a little shudder. You put your palm against it, then take it away. You do not want to touch anything connected to the room below.
          <br><br>
          Someone shouts. A heavier sound cuts through it. You wait for your parents to call up that you are safe, that you should stay in bed, even that you are being silly. Nobody calls up at all.
          <br><br>
          The landing light is still on. A shadow passes across the thread beneath your door. It stops where a pair of feet ought to stop. You pull the covers to your chest and look at the handle. It remains level. You find yourself wishing it would turn, then wishing so hard that it will not turn that your teeth hurt.
          <br><br>
          The hem of your shirt is caught beneath one knee. When you try to move, it holds you for a moment. You nearly cry out. You free the cloth slowly, keeping your eyes on the door, while something drags along the other side of the wall.
          <br><br>
          Your mouth is open. You want your parent to answer. You don't want the shadow to hear you. The first sound sticks in your throat.
          <br><br>
          You look at the handle and draw breath to call. Another crash starts downstairs.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          巨响让你猛地坐起来，这才知道刚才已经睡着。楼下先有个小东西撞上地板，随后许多小东西一起响。玻璃。你摔过杯子，认得这种声音，可这次一直不停。
          <br><br>
          楼下又一扇窗碎了。床旁的墙轻轻一震。你把手掌贴上去，又立即缩回。不想碰任何与楼下房间相连的东西。
          <br><br>
          有人喊了一声。更沉的声音把叫喊截断。你等父母朝楼上说你是安全的，说该待在床上，哪怕说你在胡闹。没有人朝楼上说话。
          <br><br>
          楼梯间的灯还亮着。一道影子经过门底那根细线，停在一双脚应该停的地方。你把被子拉到胸前，盯着门把。它仍然平着。你先盼它转动，随后又用力盼它千万别转，咬得牙都疼了。
          <br><br>
          衣摆压在一边膝盖下。你一动，它把你拽住了一瞬。你差点叫出来。你慢慢抽出布，眼睛始终盯着门，墙的另一边有什么拖了过去。
          <br><br>
          你张着嘴，想听见父母回答，又不想让那道影子听见你。第一个声音卡在喉咙里。
          <br><br>
          你盯着门把手，吸进一口气，准备叫人。楼下又响起破碎声。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-listen'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('called')>>You call for your parents. Your first try is too small. You try again, and the scraping outside stops. You hear the handle dip against its latch. You pull the covers over your head before you can see whether the door opens. No familiar voice answers your call.<<else>>You keep watching the door. The shadow underneath widens until the thread of light is gone. The handle dips, very slowly. You pull the covers over your head. For one moment you can still see its shape through the cloth. Then you shut your eyes.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          The covers stick to your mouth when you breathe in. You make a little hollow with both hands and breathe into that. Your heel has slipped out at the bottom. You draw it back, afraid of touching something that was not there when you went to bed.
          <br><br>
          You remember Sydney's knock. Two, then one. You listen for it so hard that the next three sounds almost become it. The last is a heavy blow from downstairs. You cannot make yourself stop waiting for the first two to come again.
          <br><br>
          A floorboard creaks outside. Another answers it closer to the bed, or seems to. You cannot check without uncovering your face. You press your knees together to keep the mattress still. Something brushes the wood with a dry, patient sound.
          <br><br>
          You start counting between noises. You reach four before a word interrupts you. It is too close to hear properly through the cloth. You stop counting, and the next silence lasts much longer than four.
          <br><br>
          You draw air in too quickly and the fabric touches your lips. You push it away with both hands. <span class="blue">There is room to breathe if you can keep the hollow open.</span>
          <br><br>
          You hold the cloth away from your lips. A scrape reaches the foot of the bed, or seems to. You breathe as quietly as you can.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('called')>>你喊父母。第一次太轻。你又喊，外面的刮擦停了。你听见门把压下去，碰到门闩。还没看清门有没有开，你就把被子拉过头顶。没有熟悉的声音回答。<<else>>你仍盯着门。下面的影子变宽，直到那根亮线消失。门把压下去，很慢。你把被子拉过头顶。有一瞬还能隔着布看见它的形状，随后闭紧了眼。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          吸气时，被子贴住嘴。你用双手撑出一个小空洞，朝里面呼吸。一只脚跟露在被外。你赶紧缩回来，怕碰到上床时还没有的东西。
          <br><br>
          你想起悉尼的敲门声。先两下，再一下。你听得太用力，接下来的三个声音几乎就变成了它。最后那声却是楼下的重击。你没办法不再等前两声重新响起。
          <br><br>
          房外一块地板响了。另一声似乎离床更近。想看清，就得露出脸。你把双膝并紧，让床垫别动。有什么擦着木头，干燥，缓慢，不像急着离开。
          <br><br>
          你开始数两次声响之间的间隔。数到四，一个词打断了你。它太近，隔着布反而听不清。你停下数数，接下来的沉默比四长得多。
          <br><br>
          你吸气太急，被子上的布一下贴到嘴唇。你用两只手把它撑开。<span class="blue">只要能把这个小空隙留住，你就有地方呼吸。</span>
          <br><br>
          你撑着布，不让它碰到嘴唇。刮擦似乎已经到了床脚。你尽量轻轻地呼吸。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-count'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You hold the covers away from one ear without losing the hollow beneath them. There is your name, perhaps. A voice says something like "please", and another sound swallows the rest. You lift the cloth a finger's width. Cold air reaches your ear. At once something knocks against the door, and you cover it again. You heard more before you tried to listen.
          <br><br>
          You know where your parents' shoes are usually left. If one of them is walking outside, the shoes ought to knock against the boards. You listen for that ordinary noise. The next sound is softer, as though something is being pulled without being lifted.
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.known.bishop>>"Spare the child." You suddenly hear the whole phrase, the words you have made from the bishop's account years after this night. His voice cannot belong outside this door, yet the words sound near enough to touch. You press the pillow over your ear. When you lift it, the voice is gone. You cannot tell what the child heard and what you have brought here.<<else>>You try to keep one sentence in your head for tomorrow. Each time you repeat it, a different word fits. You are afraid that an adult will ask what you heard, and that you will have to choose one.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          The handle moves again. You hear the latch catch. You picture your parent standing outside, one hand on the handle. Then a scrape runs along the bottom of the door. In your head, the hand slips lower.
          <br><br>
          <span class="green">The cloth no longer sticks to your mouth when you breathe.</span> You keep both hands in place. Someone speaks outside, too softly for you to make out the words.
          <br><br>
          One finger finds a loose stitch. You hook it through the thread. When the floor creaks again, you pull until the thread bites into your skin, but you do not let go.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你撑开一边耳朵上的被子，仍留着下面的小空洞。也许是你的名字。有个声音说了像“求你”的话，剩下的被另一声响吞没。你把布抬起一指宽，冷空气碰到耳朵。立刻有什么撞上门，你又盖了回去。没试着听之前，反而听得更多。
          <br><br>
          你知道父母平时把鞋留在哪里。假如外面走的是他们，鞋底应该敲在木板上。你想听见那个普通的声音。下一声却更轻，像有什么一直被拖着，没有抬起来。
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.known.bishop>>“放过孩子。”整句话突然清晰了。这是你从多年后主教的讲述里拼出的句子。门外不该有他的声音，可这些字近得仿佛能碰到。你把枕头压在耳朵上。再抬起时，声音消失了。你分不清哪些是孩子听到的，哪些是你带进来的。<<else>>你想把一句话留在脑海里，明天好说。每重复一次，就有另一个词能填进去。你怕大人问听见了什么，怕到时候必须选一个。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          门把又动了。你听见门闩卡住，想象父母就站在外面，一只手握着把手。随后，刮擦沿着门的下沿响起。脑海里的那只手也跟着往下滑。
          <br><br>
          <span class="green">呼吸时，布不再贴上嘴了。</span>你把双手留在原处。外面有人说话，声音太轻，听不清说了什么。
          <br><br>
          一根手指摸到松脱的那针线，你把它勾住。地板再次响起时，你拉得线勒进皮肤，却没有松手。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-choke'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>

          The cloth closes against your mouth. You suck at it once before understanding why <span class="red">no air comes</span>. Your knees kick the frame. Outside, a movement stops at the sound.

          <br><br>

          You get two fingers between your lips and the cover, and pull. Air comes with a little sob you cannot hide. The shadow below the door thickens. You clamp your lips shut and stay still until you can breathe without kicking.
          <br><br>
          "I don't know," you whisper into the space between your hands. The words are swallowed by the cloth. You say them again, louder, and hear a scrape outside. You hold your breath until it passes.

          <br><br>

          There is a loose stitch near the edge of the cover. You hook a finger through it. The thread hurts when you pull, but it stays where you left it. You find it again whenever a noise makes you forget which way you are facing.

          <br><br>

          The bed gives a small jolt. Perhaps you have kicked its frame. You hold both feet above the sheet until your legs ache. Nothing jolts it again. You lower them a little at a time, waiting after each movement.

          <br><br>

          You need the toilet. You try not to think about the bare floor, the handle, the distance to the next door. You decide to wait for your parent. Then you decide to wait until the landing is quiet. It becomes quiet, and you still cannot leave the bed.

          <br><br>

          At some point the darkness inside the covers turns grey. You do not remember sleeping. You uncover one eye first. The door is closed, your shirt is twisted again, and there is no one beside the bed to tell you whether it is safe to get up.
        <<option 'CN'>>

          布贴住了你的嘴。你先用力吸了一次，随后才明白，为什么<span class="red">一直吸不到气</span>。膝盖踢中了床架。外面那阵移动的声音，循着这一响停了下来。

          <br><br>

          你把两根手指挤进嘴唇和被子之间，用力往外拉。空气终于进来，也带出一声藏不住的抽泣。门下的影子更浓了。你抿紧嘴唇，一动不动，直到不再踢腿也能呼吸。
          <br><br>
          你对双手之间的小空隙轻声说：“我不知道。”布吞掉了这些字。你又说一次，大声一点，外面便响起刮擦。你屏住气，等它过去。

          <br><br>

          被子边缘有一针松线。你把手指勾进去。拉紧时有点疼，可线仍在留下的位置。每次声响让你忘了自己朝哪边，你就再找一次。

          <br><br>

          床轻轻震了一下。也许是你踢到了床架。你把两只脚悬在床单上方，直到腿酸。床没再震。你一点一点放下，每动一次都等一会儿。

          <br><br>

          你想去厕所。你努力不去想地板、门把，以及到下一扇门的距离。你决定等父母来，再决定等楼梯间安静。终于安静了，你却仍然离不开床。

          <br><br>

          不知什么时候，被子里的黑变成灰。你记不得睡过。先露出一只眼。门关着，上衣又拧住了，床边没有人告诉你现在能不能下床。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-grey'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You wake expecting to be late for breakfast. You listen for the cupboard door, a spoon against a bowl, the voice that will tell you how much time you have wasted. The house waits with you.
          <br><br>
          You put one foot out, then pull it back when a board creaks. The collar of your shirt is damp. You tug it away from your neck and look at the door, waiting for a second creak. It does not come.
          <br><br>
          The handle turns normally. You open the door a little and find the landing where it ought to be. No one is there. A piece of glass catches the morning light on the first stair. There are more on the next one. You cannot see whether any have reached the bottom of the stairs.
          <br><br>
          You tie your trainers tightly and choose the parts of each step you can see. Halfway down, the banister shifts under your hand. You freeze. Something breathes from the upper passage behind you, and you wait until its next breath before you move your foot.
          <br><br>
          You look for a clear place to put your feet. Usually someone would tell you off for coming down before you were called. You pause on the stair, waiting for that voice.
          <br><br>
          At the last stair, you stop. You can see a piece of ordinary bread on the table. Yesterday somebody would have swept the glass before asking you to come down.
          <br><br>
          You put your foot where you can see the board and feel the sole meet it. There is still a whole shoe between you and the broken things. The next breath comes from upstairs. You look towards the bread, then turn back. You climb to the upper passage again, keeping your hand near the rail's post. Your parents' door is beside the family portrait, not down here among the empty chairs.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你醒来，以为自己又要赶不上早餐。你听着柜门、勺子碰碗，还有会告诉你已经耽搁多久的声音。房子和你一起等。
          <br><br>
          你先伸出一只脚，一块木板响了，又赶紧缩回来。上衣领口潮了。你把它拉得离脖子远一点，看着门，等第二声木板响。没有来。
          <br><br>
          门把照常转动。你把门开一点，楼梯间还在该在的位置，没人。第一阶上有片玻璃映着晨光，下一阶还有。你看不见它们有没有一直落到楼梯底下。
          <br><br>
          你系紧运动鞋，挑每一阶看得清的地方落脚。走到一半，扶手在掌下动了。你僵住。身后的上层过道传来呼吸，你等到下一口气响起，才挪动脚。
          <br><br>
          你找能落脚的空处。平时，没等人叫就下楼，总要挨一句训。你停在楼梯上，等着那个声音。
          <br><br>
          走到最后一级楼梯，你又停下来。桌上还能看见一片普通的面包。窗户破掉以前，会先有人把玻璃扫净，再叫你下来吃。
          <br><br>
          你把脚慢慢放到能看清的木板上，感觉鞋底确实碰到了它。至少，在你和那些破碎的东西之间，还隔着一整只鞋。下一口呼吸又从楼上传来。你望向面包，随后还是转回身，扶着靠近柱子的那段栏杆，重新爬到上层过道。父母的房门就在全家画像旁，不在楼下那些空椅子之间。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-landing'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          The upper passage is not empty. There is breathing beyond your parents' door, beside the family portrait. Sometimes it seems to come from the boards themselves. You cannot hear whether there are two breaths or one breath with a pause in the middle.
          <br><br>
          A chair lies on its side beside the narrow table. You know the scrape on its leg from dragging it to the upstairs window to look down at the garden. You nearly put it upright before seeing the grooves cut into the wood beside it. You set your hand back against your own leg instead.
          <br><br>
          No one is beside the narrow table. A broken cup lies underneath it. You look for its handle. It would be easier if you could recognise one broken thing. From the bedroom, a scrape moves towards the door, and you stop looking.
          <br><br>
          You call once. The breathing stops. You wait for your name, but only the breathing returns, much closer to the bottom of the door.
          <br><br>
          Both the kitchen and the front entrance are downstairs. To reach either, you have to turn away from this door and get back to the stairs. There is room beside the overturned chair if you turn sideways. You can call from here, or keep your shoulder against the opposite wall and try to get past before anything hears your soles on the glass.
          <br><br>
          The kitchen window is bright downstairs. You remember the bread on the table. Behind this door, the breathing catches and starts again.
          <br><br>
          "It's me." You have not said it yet. You look from the door to the narrow table. There is just enough room to stand behind it.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          上层过道并不是空的。全家画像旁，父母的房门后传来呼吸，有时像从脚下木板本身传出来。你听不出是两口气，还是一口中间停了停的气。
          <br><br>
          窄桌旁倒着一把椅子。你认得椅腿上的擦痕，以前把它拖到楼上窗前、往下看花园时，就弄出了这道痕迹。你差点去扶，随后看见旁边木头上刻出的深沟。你把手收回来，贴在自己的腿上。
          <br><br>
          窄桌旁没有人，桌下躺着一只碎掉的杯子。你找它的把手。要是能认出一样碎掉的东西，事情似乎会容易些。卧室里，刮擦朝房门靠过来，你不再找了。
          <br><br>
          你喊了一声。呼吸停了。你等着自己的名字，却只有呼吸回来，贴近门的下沿。
          <br><br>
          厨房和前门都在楼下，要去任何一处，都得先离开这扇门，回到楼梯口。倒着的椅子旁还有一点空隙，侧身能走。你可以站在这里喊，也可以把肩贴在另一边墙上，试着赶在有什么听见鞋底擦过玻璃前过去。
          <br><br>
          楼下的厨房窗户很亮，你想起桌上的面包。这扇门后，呼吸顿住，又重新响起。
          <br><br>
          “是我。”你还没有说出口。你看看门，又看看窄桌。桌后刚好还够站。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-door'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You knock once. Usually you would knock again before waiting. Today the first tap is answered by movement so low down that you look at your feet.
          <br><br>
          Nothing tells you to come in. You press your palm to the wood. You think of illness, of the times you were allowed into this room when you could not sleep. "It's me."
          <br><br>
          The door moves under your hand. You have pushed it. A strip of the master bedroom appears: the four-poster bed, with its covers still in place. Its posts are whole. The chair beside it is pieces. The cupboard is open in places where a cupboard should not open. Splinters and old fabric cover the carpet.
          <br><br>
          You cannot see anyone lying on the bed. The breathing comes from below it.
          <br><br>
          You try your name again. The sound underneath stops. Something rubs against the carpet. The room is dark below the covers, even where morning light ought to reach. You keep one foot outside the threshold and your hand on the handle. If you let go, you will have to find it again without looking away from the bed.
          <br><br>
          Your arm is not long enough to hold the handle and remain against the opposite wall. You have to step nearer. You move only as far as the wood requires.
          <br><br>
          The sheet under the bed lifts, then drops. You want to call it a draught. You wait for the window curtain to move as well. It does not.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你只敲一下。平时，还没开始等，你就会再敲。今天，第一声才响，就有动静回应，位置低得让你看向自己的脚。
          <br><br>
          没有声音让你进去。你把手掌贴在木头上，想起生病，想起以前睡不着时可以进这个房间。“是我。”
          <br><br>
          门在掌下动了，是你推的。主卧露出一条缝：四帷柱大床，被子还在原处。床柱完好，旁边的椅子却成了碎块。柜子在不该打开的地方裂开。地毯上全是木刺和旧布。
          <br><br>
          床上看不见躺着的人。呼吸从床下面来。
          <br><br>
          你又说了一遍自己的名字。下面的声音停了，有什么擦着地毯。被单下很黑，连晨光该照到的地方也黑。你留一只脚在门槛外，手仍握着门把。松开，就得在不能把目光从床边移开的情况下重新找到它。
          <br><br>
          你的胳膊没有那么长，没办法一边握住门把手，一边仍贴着对面的墙。你必须再靠近一点。你只挪动了开门所需要的那段距离，不肯多迈一步。
          <br><br>
          床下垂着的被单抬起来，又落回去。你很想说，那只是穿堂风。你等着窗帘也跟着动一动，好证明自己是对的。窗帘却始终没有动。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-parent'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          A hand comes out before you see the face. Its fingers spread against the carpet. At their ends, something silver catches the light. You look for a ring, then realise the silver is where the nails should be.
          <br><br>
          A gaunt face lifts beneath the hanging sheet. Pale eyes find you. It has scraps of black cloth around it. You cannot tell which parent it is. You cannot tell whether the breathing farther back belongs to someone else.
          <br><br>
          "Are you ill?"
          <br><br>
          The hand moves at the sound. You know the little impatient tap of a finger, the one you used to hear beside a plate when you were slow sitting down. Then the nails press into the carpet and the whole arm pulls forward. You step back. The head stops, but the hand does not.
          <br><br>
          It reaches the threshold just as you lift your foot. A nail touches the side of your shoe. You pull free without waiting to see whether it meant to hold you. The skin behind the silver looks colder than the floor you are standing on.
          <br><br>
          You back into the upper passage, still facing the bed. The figure withdraws. The familiar finger taps once more in the dark. You want to answer it. You keep moving until there is a wall between you and that hand.
          <br><br>
          You stop by the chair with your heart so loud that the next breath is lost beneath it. You look at your shoe where the nail touched. Nothing has gone through the sole.
          <br><br>
          "Are you ill?" You mouth the question again. The tapping stops. You back away from the bedroom without waiting for an answer.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你先看见手，才看见脸。手指在地毯上张开，尖端有银色映着光。你想找戒指，随后明白银色长在本该是指甲的地方。
          <br><br>
          垂下的床单下面抬起一张憔悴的脸。苍白的眼睛找到你，周围挂着黑色破布。你认不出是哪位父母，也听不出更深处的呼吸是不是来自另一个。
          <br><br>
          “你病了吗？”
          <br><br>
          手循着声音动了。你认得那种不耐烦地轻敲一下的动作，以前坐下吃饭太慢，盘边就会响起它。随后指甲按进地毯，整条手臂拉了出来。你退一步。头停了，手没停。
          <br><br>
          你抬脚时，它正好够到门槛。一根指甲碰到鞋侧。你赶紧抽回，没等看清它是不是想抓住。银色后面的皮肤，看起来比脚下地板还冷。
          <br><br>
          你仍朝着床，退回上层过道。那个身影缩了回去，熟悉的手指在暗处又敲一下。你想回答，却一直退到墙把你和那只手隔开。
          <br><br>
          你在椅子旁停下，心跳响得让你听不见接下来的一口呼吸。你低头查看指甲刚才碰过的那只鞋，没有东西扎穿鞋底。
          <br><br>
          “你病了吗？”你无声地又问了一次。轻敲停了。你没有等回答，继续往卧室外退。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-pantry'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          Downstairs, you reach the kitchen. The cupboard catches against something on the floor. You pull, stop at the noise, then pull again. It opens. Inside are bread, jars, the things that were there yesterday. You hold a loaf against your chest for a moment before putting it on the counter.
          <br><br>
          <<if !$LostLamb.marks.includes('saw-parent')>>You keep watching the stairs. On the way down, you passed the bedroom without looking inside. A pale hand slid into the upper passage behind you, its silver nails raking the boards where your heel had just been. You ran down the remaining stairs and put the kitchen table between yourself and its doorway. You saw no face, and nothing followed you down. Only when the scraping stopped above could you release the chair you had gripped.<br><br><</if>>
          The knife is in its usual place. You put it down twice before your hand will hold it steadily. There is nobody to cut the bread, and the loaf does not become smaller however long you look at it. You start with one end, keeping your fingers far from the blade.
          <br><br>
          You have not eaten. A scrape from upstairs makes you drop a piece onto the counter. You wait. You pick it up when the scrape stops.
          <br><br>
          Three plates fit beside one another. You know how much went on each yesterday. You do not know whether your parents can eat it now. Preparing only your own would be quicker. Preparing theirs would mean climbing back to that doorway with both hands full.
          <br><br>
          The first thing you find that has not changed is a jar lid that will not turn. You try twice and give up, annoyed. There is bread that does not need a lid opened.
          <br><br>
          Your hunger has not waited for an adult to explain the room. You can feel it pulling below your ribs. <span class="blue">Eating first would steady your hands. Making every portion first would keep them occupied longer.</span>
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你下楼走进厨房，柜门却被地上的东西卡住。你拉一下，因为声音停住，又拉。开了。里面有面包、罐子，都是昨天还在的东西。你把一条面包抱在胸前一会儿，才放上柜台。
          <br><br>
          <<if !$LostLamb.marks.includes('saw-parent')>>你仍盯着楼梯。刚才下楼时，你没有往卧室里看，直接经过了门口。身后一只苍白的手滑进上层过道，银色指甲刮过刚才脚跟还踩着的木板。你跑完剩下的阶梯，把厨房桌子挡在自己和厨房门口之间。你没有看见脸，也没有什么跟着你下楼。直到上面的刮擦停住，你才放得开一直抓着的椅子。<br><br><</if>>
          刀还在平时的位置。你放下两次，手才握得稳。没人切面包，你看多久，它都不会变小。你从一端切起，让手指远离刀刃。
          <br><br>
          你还没吃东西。楼上的刮擦让一块面包从掌中掉上柜台。你等着，刮擦停了才捡起来。
          <br><br>
          三只盘子并排放得下。你知道昨天每只里放多少，不知道现在父母还能不能吃。只准备自己的会快一点。准备他们的，就得双手都端着东西，重新爬到那扇门前。
          <br><br>
          你找到的第一件没有变的东西，是一个依然拧不开的罐子。你试了两次，恼火地放弃了。旁边还有面包，不需要先拧开任何盖子，就能吃。
          <br><br>
          饥饿没有等一个大人过来，解释那间屋子怎么了。它已经在你的肋骨下面不停拉扯。<span class="blue">先吃一点，双手就会稳一些。先把每个人的份都做好，它们就得忙更久。</span>
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-eat'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You cut the piece for yourself first. It feels like taking something before you have been told to. You stand at the counter, with the bread in one hand and the other pressed against the wood, until hunger makes the decision you cannot.
          <br><br>
          The first mouthful is dry. You take too much water with it, cough, and clamp a hand over your mouth. Nothing comes into the kitchen. After a while you eat the next mouthful. This one goes down.
          <br><br>
          You remember the strips of pastry your parent left to cool. You had wanted yours before it was ready. Now you would wait as long as they asked if they would come in and ask. The bread has a torn place where the nick in the knife caught it. You pick a little crumb from it and eat that too.
          <br><br>
          Your stomach stops pulling so hard. The cup stays level when you lift it. You line up three plates and cut two more pieces, watching the staircase after each stroke.
          <br><br>
          A little sound comes from the bedroom upstairs. You stop with the knife flat against the loaf. It is not the sound of someone calling you greedy. You make yourself put the knife down before turning.
          <br><br>
          You cut the remaining pieces, one larger than the other, because you know how they used to be. Then you put the cup where your elbow will not knock it. The table is a place you can return to now, with some food still on it. You lift the first plate, leaving the other hand empty.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你先给自己切了一片。还没有人说可以，拿走这片面包就像偷了什么似的。你站在柜台边，一只手握着面包，另一只手抵住木头，迟迟没有动。最后，是饥饿替你做了那个自己一直做不出的决定。
          <br><br>
          第一口干得咽不下去。你急着喝水，一下喝得太多，咳了起来，赶紧用手捂住嘴。厨房门口没有出现什么。过了一会儿，你才敢吃下一口。这一次，面包终于咽下去了。
          <br><br>
          你想起父母曾经放在一边晾凉的酥皮。那时，你总想趁它还没准备好就先吃。现在，只要对方能走进厨房，亲口让你等，无论等多久，你都愿意。刀刃上的缺口把面包扯破了一小块。你从那里抠下一点碎屑，也放进了嘴里。
          <br><br>
          肚子不再揪得那么疼了。你举起杯子，水面也不再晃得那么厉害。你排好三只盘子，再切两块，每下切一刀，都先往楼梯看一眼。
          <br><br>
          楼上的卧室里响起一点动静。你停下来，刀刃还平贴着面包。那并不是有人在喊你贪吃。你先让自己把刀放下，随后才转过头去。
          <br><br>
          剩下的两块，你切得一大一小，因为以前就是这样分的。你把杯子挪到手肘碰不到的位置。现在，这张桌子至少还有食物留着，等你回来。你举起第一只盘子，把另一只手空出来。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-share'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You set out three plates. Your own is the small one. You turn the others until they face the empty chairs, then realise they will not be eaten here. You turn them back. The plates look wrong whichever way they face.
          <br><br>
          The knife sticks partway through the loaf. You have seen an adult lift it and bring it down harder. You try that, and the board moves. You put it flat again, move your fingers away, and work slowly. When the slice comes free, it is thick at one end and almost nothing at the other.
          <br><br>
          "That'll do," you say, trying out the voice you would have heard.
          <br><br>
          It does not sound like either of your parents. You cut the next piece without saying it again. You want to get the portions right. You are afraid that something about this morning might still be your fault if you get them wrong.
          <br><br>
          You stop to drink. The cup knocks against a plate. For a moment every sound in the house seems to have heard it. You stand motionless until your stomach makes an ordinary noise of its own. That noise is almost funny. You cannot laugh at it yet.
          <br><br>
          All three portions are there at last. You touch one with a fingertip to check it is real, then take your finger away, annoyed with yourself. A parent would tell you not to touch everyone's food. Yesterday you would have argued that it was your bread too.
          <br><br>
          You leave yours on the counter. You can come back for it. Carrying the plate through the hall and up the stairs, you watch the bread slide with each small movement. You put your elbow close to your side so it will stop sliding, and try to remember where your next foot ought to land.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你在柜台上摆出三只盘子，把最小的留给自己。另外两只被你转向空着的椅子。过了一会儿，你才想起，这顿饭不会有人坐在那里吃，于是又把它们转了回来。无论盘子朝着哪一边，看起来都不对。
          <br><br>
          刀切到一半，卡在面包里。你见过大人把刀抬起来，再更用力地落下。你学着试了一次，案板却也跟着动了。你重新把它放平，让手指远离刀刃，一点一点往下切。面包片终于脱开时，一头厚得很，另一头却薄得几乎没有了。
          <br><br>
          “这样就行了。”你试着学那句本来该听到的话。
          <br><br>
          说出来，却不像任何一位父母的声音。你没有再学，直接开始切下一片。你很想把三份食物分得正确，仿佛只要分错，这个早晨发生的某件事就仍然可以算作你的错。
          <br><br>
          你停下来喝水，杯沿不小心碰了盘子。有那么一刻，你觉得整座房子里的声音都听见了这一响。你站着不敢动，直到肚子自己发出了一声再普通不过的咕噜。那个声音甚至有点好笑，你却还笑不出来。
          <br><br>
          三份终于都做好了。你用指尖碰了一下其中一片，想确认它是真的，随后立刻收回手，有些恼自己。父母以前会说，别随便碰大家的食物。昨天之前，你还会争辩，这明明也是自己的面包。
          <br><br>
          你把自己那份留在柜台上，想着回来还能吃。端着盘子经过大厅，再慢慢上楼时，面包随着每一个细小的动作滑动。你把手肘紧贴在身侧，尽量让盘子端稳，努力记起下一只脚应该落在哪里。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-feed'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>

          Upstairs, beside the portrait, the bedroom door stands open a little. You use your elbow to push it wider and keep it there. The four-poster bed has not moved. Beneath it, black cloth shifts with a breath. You crouch outside the threshold and put the plate down.
          <br><br>
          "It's bread. I made it."
          <br><br>
          You used to say that when you wanted them to notice your help. You wait for a reply. The breathing grows faster. A hand comes out, feeling along the carpet. Silver points stop short of the plate, then search sideways towards your foot.
          <br><br>
          You move your foot back. The hand follows the sound, leaving the bread where it is. You remember a thumb steadying your cup at supper until you had pulled your sleeve back. Now you wait for these fingers to stop moving before you dare bend your knee.
          <br><br>
          You could push the plate close enough for the hand to find it. You could remain by the door and let it come forward. <span class="red">There is nothing heavy between your knee and those nails.</span>
          <br><br>
          You cannot make your voice sound as though this is a normal breakfast. You stop trying before it gets louder. The hand is finding each sound you make. <span class="blue">You can slide the plate without calling again.</span>
          <br><br>
          There is one clear place beside your knees. You keep your weight over it while waiting for the silver to turn away from your sleeve.
        <<option 'CN'>>

          楼上，画像旁的卧室门开着一点。你用手肘推宽，抵在那里。四帷柱大床没动，下面的黑布随呼吸起伏。你在门槛外蹲下，放下盘子。
          <br><br>
          “是面包。我做的。”
          <br><br>
          以前想让父母注意你帮了忙，就会这样说。你等回答。呼吸变快，一只手伸出来，沿着地毯摸索。银色尖端没够到盘子，随后往旁边找，朝着你的脚。
          <br><br>
          你把脚挪远。手跟着声音，将面包留在原处。你想起晚饭时贴着杯柄的拇指，一直扶到你把袖子收回。如今，你得等这些手指不再动，才敢弯膝。
          <br><br>
          你可以把盘子推到手能找到的地方，也可以留在门边，等它自己往前。<span class="red">膝盖和那些指甲之间，没有任何沉重的东西挡着。</span>
          <br><br>
          你怎么也没办法，把声音装成这只是一顿普通早餐。你赶在它变得更响之前，放弃继续尝试。那只手正在寻找你每次出声的位置。<span class="blue">你可以不再叫人，只把盘子滑过去。</span>
          <br><br>
          膝盖旁还有一小块没有东西的地方。你把身体的重量留在那里，耐心等着那些银色的指甲从自己的袖口转开。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-food-quiet'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          The plate slides out of your reach. You have kept your fingers behind its rim. When the silver nails come down, <span class="green">they catch porcelain</span>.
          <br><br>
          You almost take it back. It is your parent's good plate, the one you have been told not to drop. The thought is so ordinary that for a moment you are more afraid of breaking it than of the hand. You stop reaching. A long, dry breath comes from beneath the bed.
          <br><br>
          The bread moves into the dark. You cannot see a mouth. You hear one short sound, then another, and realise you have been staring hard enough to make your eyes water. You look at the carpet beside your foot instead. It is worn where adults used to stand to put their shoes on.
          <br><br>
          "There's more," you say, softly enough that you are not sure you said it aloud.
          <br><br>
          No answer comes. The plate is drawn farther in. For a moment there is only the sheet, moving with a breath. You move into the upper passage before the hand needs another thing to find, then go downstairs to the kitchen. It does not follow.
          <br><br>
          You wait at the foot of the stairs. Nothing calls after you. You nearly shout that you brought breakfast, then hear the plate scrape against the floor above. You go back to your own food.
          <br><br>
          From the kitchen you can see the garden doorway without crossing the spilled glass. The breathing has settled in the bedroom upstairs. <span class="blue">For now, that side of the hall is free.</span> You remember where the free space begins. If you want to leave, you can use it before the sound changes place.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你把盘子滑到自己够不到的地方，手指始终藏在盘沿后面。银色的指甲落下来，<span class="green">勾住的是瓷器</span>。
          <br><br>
          你差一点又伸手把它拿回来。那是父母珍惜的盘子，以前总有人嘱咐你不要摔坏。这个念头太熟悉了，有那么一瞬间，你怕盘子碎掉，甚至比怕那只手还多。你硬是停住了手。床下传来一口又长又干的呼吸。
          <br><br>
          面包被拖进黑暗。你看不见嘴，只听见短短的一声，随后又是一声。眼睛酸起来，你才发现自己一直死死盯着。你改看脚旁的地毯，那一小块已经磨旧，以前大人会站在那里穿鞋。
          <br><br>
          “还有。”你轻轻地说，声音小得连自己都不确定有没有真正说出口。
          <br><br>
          没有回答。盘子被拉向更深处。片刻之间，你只能看见被单随着呼吸起伏。你赶在那只手开始寻找下一样东西之前，退到上层过道，再下楼回到厨房。它没有跟来。
          <br><br>
          你在楼梯底下等，没有声音叫住你。你差点喊，自己把早餐送来了，楼上却只响起盘子擦过地板的声音。你回去吃自己的那份。
          <br><br>
          从厨房这里，你能看见通向花园的门，不必经过那片散落的玻璃。呼吸暂时停在楼上的卧室里，<span class="blue">大厅靠花园的那一侧还没有动静。</span>你记住空出来的路从哪里开始。如果要离开，现在就可以趁声音还没有换位置，先从那边走过去。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-food-spill'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You try to slide the plate while speaking. The last word comes out louder than the first. The hand changes direction before the bread reaches it.
          <br><br>
          <span class="red">Cold flesh closes over the rim and your cuff together.</span> You pull once, and a silver nail catches a thread. The plate tilts. You try to keep it level with your other hand, bringing that wrist close as well. You stop before it reaches the fingers underneath the sheet.
          <br><br>
          "I can get more."
          <br><br>
          You say it quickly, as though that could keep somebody from being angry. The hand stops moving for a moment. A face rises where you would once have expected a nod. You recognise it before you want to. The pale eyes are on your mouth.
          <br><br>
          You stop talking. The grip has not become looser. Your wrist grows cold through the sleeve, and the plate has become too heavy to hold this way. The bread slides towards the dark. You want to keep one slice from falling, to stop this from becoming another mess.
          <br><br>
          Then the nail catches the thread again. The sleeve draws tight above your fingers. You cannot save the bread and take the arm away at the same time. You move your free hand back to the doorframe, where it can hold something that will not close over it.
          <br><br>
          The porcelain rests against two nails. If you open your fingers, the plate will fall away from your hand. The cuff might tear. You watch the loose thread rather than the face, trying to find the movement that will leave your arm on this side of the threshold.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你一边说话，一边试着把盘子往前滑。最后一个字比第一个字响。面包还没滑到那只手边，它就先改了方向。
          <br><br>
          <span class="red">冰冷的皮肤把盘沿和你的袖口一起握住。</span>你拉了一下，一根银色指甲勾住衣服上的线。盘子歪了。你想用另一只手把它扶平，连那边的手腕也带近了一点。赶在它碰到被单下面的指头之前，你停住了。
          <br><br>
          “我还能再拿一些。”
          <br><br>
          你急着说出口，像是这样就能让谁不要生气。那只手有一瞬间不再挪动。一张脸从以前本该有人点头的位置抬起。你还没愿意认出它，就已经认出来了。苍白的眼睛望着你的嘴。
          <br><br>
          你不敢再讲话。那只手却没有松。隔着袖子，手腕越来越冷，盘子也重得让你难以继续这样拿住。面包开始往黑暗里滑。你还想保住其中一片，不让这里又变得一团糟。
          <br><br>
          指甲再次勾住了那根线。手指上方的袖子绷紧了。你没办法既保住面包，又把胳膊抽开。你把空着的那只手收回，放到门框上。至少那块木头不会合拢，将手也抓在里面。
          <br><br>
          瓷器抵着两根指甲。只要你张开手，盘子就会从掌中落下，袖口也可能因此撕开。你没有再看那张脸，只盯着松脱的线，努力想出怎样动，才能让自己的胳膊留在门槛这一边。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-clear'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You are back downstairs, within reach of the kitchen table. <<if !$LostLamb.marks.includes('path') and !$LostLamb.marks.includes('had-water') and !$LostLamb.marks.includes('outside-view')>>The brush is taller than you want it to be. You move it from one hand to the other, looking at the hall, the sink and the patch of sunlight near the garden doorway. All three places seem to want something from you at once.
          <br><br>
          You have not been asked to do a chore. There is no adult to tell you which part matters most. Your feet need somewhere to go. Your mouth is dry. Outside, a cart rattles past and someone shouts an ordinary greeting. You want to be where that person is.
          <br><br>
          You put the brush down without letting it fall. There are still things you can do from this side of the table. You look at them one at a time. The bedroom sound does not stop while you decide.<</if>>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('path')>>
          <br><br>
          The clear strip runs beside the wall. You can fit both feet on it now. You have left the brush flat so it will not fall across the place you worked for. Going out will be easier, although you cannot make the upstairs room quiet.
          <</if>>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('had-water')>>
          <br><br>
          The cup is within reach. You swallow once without it, checking that your throat no longer hurts. Your fingers do not tremble as much when you rest them on the table. You are still afraid, but standing has stopped being so difficult.
          <</if>>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('outside-view')>>
          <br><br>
          You have seen the street. Someone beyond the gate is putting a bag down. You put your hand to your throat and try to call. The first sound comes out too softly to reach them.
          <</if>>
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-offer-pass') and !$LostLamb.marks.includes('path')>>The garden side is still free. <span class="blue">You can leave without sweeping first.</span><<elseif !$LostLamb.marks.includes('path')>><span class="blue">A strip beside the wall would let you reach the entrance without stepping on the glass.</span><<else>>You could use the strip now. You could drink, or look outside first, while there is still daylight.<</if>>
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你已经回到楼下，厨房的餐桌仍在够得到的位置。<<if !$LostLamb.marks.includes('path') and !$LostLamb.marks.includes('had-water') and !$LostLamb.marks.includes('outside-view')>>刷子比你希望的还要高。你把它从一只手换到另一只，看着大厅、水槽，还有花园门附近的一片日光。三个地方仿佛同时都在等着，让你去做点什么。
          <br><br>
          没有人给你布置家务，也没有大人告诉你，哪一件事最要紧。双脚需要一条能够走的路，嘴里又干得难受。外面有车经过，谁喊了一声普通的招呼。你想站到那个喊话的人所在的地方。
          <br><br>
          你把刷子放下，没有让它摔在地上。桌子这一侧，你仍然能做几件事情。你一个一个看过去。即使你还没决定好，卧室里的动静也没有停。<</if>>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('path')>>
          <br><br>
          清出来的窄路贴着墙往前延伸，现在够两只脚一起站。刷子被你平放在旁边，免得它倒下，又堵住这块费力清出的地方。出去会容易一点，可楼上那间房并不会因此安静。
          <</if>>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('had-water')>>
          <br><br>
          杯子留在伸手能够到的位置。你没拿它，先自己咽了一次，确认喉咙已经不那么疼。手指搁到桌面上时，也没有抖得那么厉害。你仍然害怕，不过，站稳已经不再那么难。
          <</if>>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('outside-view')>>
          <br><br>
          你已经看过街道。门外有人正在放下袋子。你用手贴着喉咙，试着喊。第一声太轻了，没有传到那边。
          <</if>>
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-offer-pass') and !$LostLamb.marks.includes('path')>>花园那一侧还没有动静。<span class="blue">你可以不用先扫，就从那里出去。</span><<elseif !$LostLamb.marks.includes('path')>><span class="blue">沿墙清出一条窄路，就能不踩上玻璃，走到入口附近。</span><<else>>你现在就能走那条窄路。也可以趁天还亮，先喝点水，或者往外看一眼。<</if>>
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-sweep'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You begin beside the wall, where your shoes can already stand. The brush stays ahead of your toes. Glass turns beneath it, showing edges that looked like shadow a moment ago. You do not push hard enough to make the pieces scatter into another place you cannot see.
          <br><br>
          A shard rings against the lowest stair. Something moves on the landing above. You stop with the brush still on the floor. The next breath comes closer to the head of the stairs, then draws away. You wait for one more before moving the brush again.
          <br><br>
          The strip grows a little at a time. You test the first part with one shoe, keeping the other where it was. The sole does not slide. You work from there rather than reach for the far end you would like to clear. When both feet fit on the new part, you move them together.
          <br><br>
          Your sleeve rubs against the handle. <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-offer-fail')>>A thread hangs from the place where the nail caught it. You touch the skin beneath, then try each finger. All of them move. The coat button is still there beside the tear. You leave it fastened, although you want to pull the whole sleeve off.<<else>>Dust from the doorframe has marked the cuff. You brush it away with your thumb. A sound in the hall makes you flinch and brush again, as if the dust has come back while you were listening.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          There is room for both shoes now. You leave the brush flat and test the strip with one foot. A piece of glass rolls out of the pile. You stop it with the bristles before it can reach your sole.
          <br><br>
          You look along the wall to the entrance. It is farther along the ground-floor wall than the foot of the stairs you have been watching. You can walk towards it without putting your feet on the broken glass. You rub your palm once along your coat, then leave the brush where you can reach it if you need to come back.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你从靠墙、双脚已经能够站稳的地方开始扫，让刷子始终留在脚尖前面。玻璃被翻动时，刚才还像影子的地方露出了锋利的边。你没有用力推得太猛，免得这些碎片又散进别的看不清的位置。
          <br><br>
          一块玻璃碰响了最下面一级楼梯。上层平台有什么动了。你立刻停手，让刷子仍贴着地面。下一口呼吸靠近楼梯口，随后又往里退开。你多等了一次，才敢再次挪动刷子。
          <br><br>
          窄路一点一点空出来。你先用一只鞋试探最早清好的那段，另一只脚留在原位。鞋底没有滑动。你从这里继续往前扫，没有直接去够最想清出来的远端。新的一段能够放下两只脚时，你才把它们一起挪过去。
          <br><br>
          袖口擦到刷柄。<<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-offer-fail')>>指甲勾过的位置垂着一根线。你摸摸下面的皮肤，随后一根一根试着动手指。它们都还能动。外套的扣子仍留在破口旁。你没有解开，虽然很想把整个袖子都从胳膊上扯掉。<<else>>门框上的灰蹭脏了袖口。你用拇指掸掉一点。大厅的声音让你猛地缩了一下，于是又掸了一次，像是刚才听着动静的时候，那点灰也重新回来了。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          路上够放下两只鞋了。你将刷子平放，先用一只脚试。玻璃堆里滚出一块碎片，你赶在它碰到鞋底以前，用刷毛拦住。
          <br><br>
          你沿着楼下的墙望向入口。它比那个一直让你盯着的楼梯底部远一些。你已经能够朝那边走，不必将双脚踩上碎玻璃。你在外套上擦了一次掌心，把刷子留在仍够得到的位置。假如需要回来，至少还能拿到它。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-wash'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          The tap coughs. You shut it at once and listen for an answer from upstairs. The pipes knock twice. Nothing comes down the stairs.
          <br><br>
          You try again with both hands on the tap. A thin stream fills the cup. You drink too fast and cough, then put your sleeve over your mouth until it stops.
          <br><br>
          The water runs over your fingers. In the bottom of the sink, your nails look long and silver. You snatch your hands away. The pale shapes move with the water, breaking into smaller ones until they go down the drain.
          <br><br>
          You hold both hands up to the window. The nails are small and uneven. A ragged edge catches your sleeve. You pick at it until it is blunt, watching the stairwell between each try.
          <br><br>
          You leave the cup beside the tap with water still in it. When you reach for it once more, your fingers close without missing the handle.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          龙头像咳嗽一样响了。你立刻关水，听楼上有没有回答。管道敲了两下，没有什么下楼。
          <br><br>
          你用两只手握着龙头再试一次，细细的水装进杯子。你喝得太快，咳了起来，便用袖子盖住嘴，直到咳嗽停下。
          <br><br>
          水流过手指。水槽底下，你的指甲又长又银。你猛地抽回双手。苍白的形状却还随水移动，碎成更小的几块，最后钻进下水口。
          <br><br>
          你举起两只手，让窗户照着。指甲很小，边缘不整齐，一片毛边勾住袖子。你把它抠钝，每试一次，就先往楼梯间看一眼。
          <br><br>
          你将杯子留在龙头边，里面还有水。再伸手一次，手指终于握住把手，没有错过。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-garden'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          The garden has kept its shape. The shrubs still crowd the narrow path. You take two quick steps, expecting Sydney to come after you, and feel foolish when you hear only your own shoes.
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('waited')>>You stop at the bend where you waited for <<nnpc_him 'Sydney'>>. The path behind it is empty. You wait for a breath anyway, then another.<<elseif $LostLamb.marks.includes('shortcut')>>You take the shortcut. A branch catches your sleeve. You wrench free too quickly, certain for an instant that it is the hand from the room.<<else>>You stay on the wider path. You keep the house on one side where you can see its doors. The narrow turn would hide them from you.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          At the gate you try the latch twice before lifting it. It has not been locked. Outside, someone carries a bag. Someone stops to adjust a shoe. They walk past the broken windows without looking up. You nearly run after them, then look back at the house.
          <br><br>
          The open garden door is a dark rectangle now. You cannot see the corridor from here. You leave the brush against the wall, where you can pick it up on the way back.
          <br><br>
          You can cross the gate. You can call from behind it. Neither will put an adult beside the bed unless you say enough to make them follow. You try the first words quietly and find that saying "my parents" is harder than lifting the latch.
          <br><br>
          You lift the latch again. It opens. Your fingers wait for something to close over them from the other side. Only the cold iron touches your palm.
          <br><br>
          You can see the street and the small space beside the wall at the same time. If you come back with someone, this is a place where both of you could wait without entering the bedroom.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          花园还保留着原来的样子。灌木仍挤着窄路。你快走两步，等悉尼追来，只听见自己的鞋，便觉得傻。
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('waited')>>你停在以前等<<nnpc_him 'Sydney'>>的转弯处。后面的路空着。你还是等一口气，又一口气。<<elseif $LostLamb.marks.includes('shortcut')>>你走了捷径。枝条勾住袖子，你挣得太急，有一瞬间确信是房里那只手。<<else>>你走宽路，让房子一直在看得见门的那一侧。窄弯会把门挡住。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          到大门前，你试了两次搭扣才抬起来。没有锁。外面有人提着包，有人停下来整理鞋。他们经过碎掉的窗户，连头也没抬。你差点跑着追去，随后又看看房子。
          <br><br>
          开着的花园门，现在是个黑色长方形。从这里看不见走廊。你把刷子靠墙留着，回来的路上能捡。
          <br><br>
          你可以跨过去，也可以隔着门喊。要让一个大人去床边，必须说够多，让对方愿意跟着。你轻声试开头几个字，发现说“我的父母”比抬起搭扣更难。
          <br><br>
          你再次抬起搭扣，门开了。手指等着另一侧有什么合拢，将它们捉住。最后碰到掌心的，只有冰凉的铁。
          <br><br>
          站在这里，你能够同时看见街道和墙边那一块窄地。假如带着别人回来，你们两个都能在这里等，不必先走进卧室。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-backgate'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You leave the brush where it is. The breathing is steady, and you move while it stays steady. The garden doorway is wider than the part of the hall beside the glass. You put a foot outside before remembering to take a coat.
          <br><br>
          The air is cold enough to make your face sting. For a moment that is a good feeling. You can see where it comes from. The wind catches the leaves, touches your ears, and moves on. Nothing in it waits for you to call a name.
          <br><br>
          You keep the house wall between yourself and the broken windows. A shutter has come loose. Each time it taps, you stop. After the third time you look up and see it moving. You wait for it to hit once more so you can believe the next sound when it comes.
          <br><br>
          At the far corner you can see the garden path. <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('shortcut')>>The little gap you raced through is still there. You take it slowly now, holding the branch aside rather than forcing through.<<elseif $LostLamb.marks.includes('waited')>>You stop at the place where you waited for Sydney. For a moment you leave room beside yourself out of habit. Then you walk on.<<else>>You follow the path without stepping between the shrubs. From here you can see both the house and the gate.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          Nobody calls you back. At the gate, that feels worse than being called. You open it and put one shoe on the pavement. The street is not the garden again. A person passing nearly walks into you, says to watch out, and continues.
          <br><br>
          You watch that person reach the corner. They do not begin walking past you again. You can follow far enough to speak, or speak to the next person. You pull the gate almost shut, keeping your fingers clear of where it will catch.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你把刷子留在原处。床下的呼吸很稳，你就趁它还没有变化，往花园门口走。那里比散落玻璃旁的那段大厅宽一些。你先把一只脚伸到外面，随后才想起自己没有拿外套。
          <br><br>
          冷空气让脸微微发刺。有那么一会儿，那反而是种好的感觉，至少你看得见它从哪里来。风吹动树叶，擦过你的耳朵，又继续往前。里面没有什么在等着你叫出一个名字。
          <br><br>
          你贴着屋外的墙走，让它挡在自己和那些碎掉的窗户之间。一扇百叶窗松脱了，每敲响一下，你就停一下。第三次，你终于抬起头，看见它正在风里晃。你特意等它再撞一次，好让下一声响起时，自己能够相信那仍然只是它。
          <br><br>
          走到远处的转角，花园小路露了出来。<<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('shortcut')>>你和悉尼比赛时钻过的小缝还在那里。这次，你慢慢走，用手把枝条拨到一边，没有像以前那样硬挤过去。<<elseif $LostLamb.marks.includes('waited')>>你停在以前等悉尼的位置，下意识地在身旁空出一点地方。过了一会儿，你才独自继续往前走。<<else>>你沿着小路走，没有钻进灌木之间。从这里，房子和大门都能同时看见。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          没有人喊你回去。到了大门边，这竟然比有人喊还令人难受。你把门打开，先将一只鞋放上人行道。街道没有重新变成花园。一位路人差点和你撞上，让你小心些，随后就继续往前走了。
          <br><br>
          你看着那人一直走到街角，没有又从你身旁重新经过。你可以跟上去说句话，也可以等下一个人。你把大门拉得几乎合上，让手指避开门会夹住的地方。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-street'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You step through the gate. A passer-by moves aside to avoid you, then stops. Bread shows through the opening of their bag. Beneath a plain coat you see the hem of temple robes, muddy from the street.
          <br><br>
          "Are you lost?"
          <br><br>
          You point back at the manor. The person follows your finger to the broken windows. "Is anyone hurt?" You shake your head, then nod. They set the bag down before asking again.
          <br><br>
          "My parents..."
          <br><br>
          Your tongue stops. The person offers a hand. Its nails are short and blunt. You look from them to the house and do not take it.
          <br><br>
          "Stay there," they say. "Show me which window."
          <br><br>
          Something moves across the upstairs window. The person looks up too late. You pull at the coat, then let go as soon as you feel how tightly you are holding it. <span class="blue">They are still watching the broken window.</span> You have a little time to say what is inside.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你跨出大门。一位路人侧身避开你，又停下来。袋子口露着面包，普通外套下面是沾了街上泥水的神殿长袍下摆。
          <br><br>
          “迷路了吗？”
          <br><br>
          你指向身后的庄园。那人顺着手指看见碎窗。“有人受伤吗？”你摇头，又点头。对方先把袋子放下，才重新问了一次。
          <br><br>
          “我的父母……”
          <br><br>
          舌头停住了。那人向你伸手，指甲短短的，边缘很钝。你看看指甲，再看看房子，没有去牵。
          <br><br>
          “先待在那里。”对方说，“指给我看，是哪扇窗？”
          <br><br>
          楼上的窗前有什么移过。那人抬头太迟，没有看见。你拽住外套，发现自己攥得太紧，便立刻松开。<span class="blue">对方仍在看那扇碎窗。</span>你还有一点时间，能够说出里面的事。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-helper'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-call-help-pass')>>"They're ill." The person asks whether an adult is with them. "They are the adults." <span class="green">They lift the bag and follow you to the gate.</span> You say to wait there. When they take another step, you say it much louder, and they stop.<<else>>"I'm waiting for someone." They tell you to wait inside the gate. You do, and the iron bars pass between you. The person takes up the bag. You pull at a loose thread on your sleeve until it bites your finger. "The windows broke last night," you say. This time they put the bag down again.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          They ask your name. "Kylar." You wait to hear it as Sydney would say it. The person just repeats the name and asks where your parents are.
          <br><br>
          You point upwards. "Under the bed."
          <br><br>
          The temple robes scrape against the gate. The person looks from your small hand to the empty windows. "How long?" You can give them a night. You cannot tell them what sort of night.
          <br><br>
          "I've only been at the temple a little while," they say, when you stare at the robes. "Let me look first." They move slowly enough for you to keep the gate between you and the house.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-call-help-pass')>>“他们病了。”那人问有没有大人陪着。“他们就是大人。”<span class="green">对方提起袋子，跟你走到大门前。</span>你让他等在这里。他又迈一步，你便喊得很响，他停下了。<<else>>“我在等人。”对方让你到大门里面等。你照做，铁栏杆移到了你们之间。那人重新提起袋子。你扯着袖子上一根松线，勒得手指疼。“窗户是昨晚碎的。”你说。这次，他又把袋子放下。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          那人问你的名字。“凯拉尔。”你等着听他像悉尼那样念出来。他却只重复了一遍，就问父母在哪里。
          <br><br>
          你向上指。“床下面。”
          <br><br>
          神殿长袍擦过大门。那人看看你的小手，又看看空荡荡的窗。“多久了？”你能告诉他是一夜，却说不出那是怎样的一夜。
          <br><br>
          你盯着长袍，他便说：“我到神殿还没有多久。我先看看。”他走得很慢，你来得及让大门始终挡在自己和房子之间。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-silent'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You open your mouth. "My parents..."
          <br><br>
          The stranger waits. A pale hand is inside your head now, although the hand in front of you has ordinary nails. You are afraid that saying the rest will make them ask you to point at it. You are afraid that they will laugh. You are afraid that they will not laugh at all.
          <br><br>
          You shake your head and say you were waiting for somebody. The words come easily because you have been waiting for somebody for so long. The stranger asks whether you know how to get home. You nod. That answer is easy too. You know every step back to the bed.
          <br><br>
          They begin to move away. You catch the strap of their bag before you decide to. They look down, startled. You let go immediately and point towards the window.
          <br><br>
          "It's broken."
          <br><br>
          They look up. From the pavement the broken panes are more obvious than you thought. Their expression changes. They ask whether anyone else is inside. You nod again, then say that your parents will not get up. You cannot say the silver, but you can say those words.
          <br><br>
          "Show me from out here," they say. They stay on the pavement while you open the gate. They are not holding your hand. They have stopped walking away.
          <br><br>
          <span class="red">You have lost the clear sentence you wanted.</span> The person does not seem to need it to see that something is wrong. They come no closer than you ask, and wait while you find the next thing you can point at. You look back at the bedroom window before leading them to the entrance.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你张开嘴。“我的父母……”
          <br><br>
          陌生人在等你说下去。你脑袋里却已经出现了一只苍白的手，尽管眼前这只手长着普通的指甲。你怕说完以后，对方就会让你把那东西指给他看。你怕这人笑，也怕这人根本笑不出来。
          <br><br>
          你摇摇头，改口说自己正在等人。这几个字倒是很容易说，因为你已经等了很久。陌生人问，你知不知道怎么回家。你点了头，这个问题也很容易。回到那张床边，每一级台阶在哪里，你都知道。
          <br><br>
          那人准备离开。你还没有想好，就已经抓住了袋子的提带。对方吃了一惊，低头看你。你立刻松开手，改为指向窗户。
          <br><br>
          “它碎了。”
          <br><br>
          对方抬起头。从人行道上看，那些破碎的窗格比你以为的还要显眼。那人的表情变了，问屋里还有没有别人。你再次点头，随后说，父母不肯起床。你仍然说不出那些银色的东西，可这几个字至少能够说出来。
          <br><br>
          “从外面给我看看。”对方说。你去打开大门，那人却仍留在人行道上，等你告诉他该看哪里。没有人牵住你的手。那个人也没有继续往远处走。
          <br><br>
          <span class="red">你丢掉了原本想说的完整句子。</span>对方似乎并不需要那句话，才能看出有事不对。你让他靠近多少，他就只靠近多少，耐心等着你找到下一样能指的东西。带着他走向入口之前，你又回头看了一眼卧室的窗户。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-entrance'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          The person waits on the step while you try the entrance. You can feel them behind you without having to keep looking. When the handle catches, you say it always catches. It comes free on the next try.
          <br><br>
          The hall is dimmer than the street. You point at the glass first, then the chair. "Don't stand there."
          <br><br>
          They move their shoe before asking why. You had expected to have to explain. A scrape reaches you down the stairwell instead. The person stops bending to look at the window and listens.
          <br><br>
          "Where are your parents?"
          <br><br>
          You point upstairs. A breath comes down the stairwell. The person calls a greeting towards the upper passage, politely, as though there might have been a quarrel about the damage. No human answer comes back. They say it again, with less certainty.
          <br><br>
          You wait for them to tell you off about the window. When they look down at you, you stare at their shoes. Both feet are beside yours, clear of the glass. You check again when another scrape comes from upstairs.
          <br><br>
          They ask you to stay by the entrance while they try the stairs. You tell them not to call loudly. They lower their voice. The scrape stops for a moment, and both of you wait for what follows it.
          <br><br>
          "I'll try the stairs first," they say. They put a foot on the lowest step, not all the way up. You remain where you can reach the outside handle. The room has another ordinary person in it now. You can still hear everything that made you leave it.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          那人在台阶上等着，你试着打开入口。不必一直回头，你也能感觉到他在身后。门把手卡住，你赶紧解释，它一直就这样。再试一次，门终于打开了。
          <br><br>
          大厅比街上暗。你先指向玻璃，随后指向椅子。“别站那里。”
          <br><br>
          对方先把鞋移开，才问你为什么。你本来以为，自己还得好好解释才行。楼梯间传下来的刮擦声却先替你作了回答。那人不再弯腰查看破窗，停下来听着。
          <br><br>
          “你的父母在哪儿？”
          <br><br>
          你指向楼上。一口呼吸顺着楼梯间传下来。对方向上层过道客气地打了声招呼，像是这里或许只是因为弄坏东西吵过一架。没有人的声音回答。他又招呼了一次，这次已经不那么确定了。
          <br><br>
          你等着他责备你，怎么把窗户弄坏了。对方低头看你，你却只盯着他的鞋。两只脚都在你旁边，没有踩着玻璃。楼上又响了一声刮擦，你再次看过去。
          <br><br>
          他让你留在入口附近，自己先试着往楼梯走。你告诉他，不要大声叫人。对方真的放低了声音。刮擦停了一瞬，你们一起等着，不知道紧接着还会传来什么。
          <br><br>
          “我先看看楼梯。”他说。他只踩上最下面一级，没有直接上楼。你仍留在能够到外面门把手的位置。房子里现在多了另一个普通人，可那些曾经让你离开的声音，仍然全都听得见。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-visitor'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You show the person the upstairs door, keeping the staircase behind you. They crouch outside the bedroom and use the brush handle to lift the sheet. Before you can tell them not to, something pale turns in the dark.
          <br><br>
          The breath catches in their throat. They drop the sheet. "Back." You obey before a hand reaches your shoulder.
          <br><br>
          The brush rolls into the room. A silver nail hooks its end. The handle turns, slowly, until it points at the hem of the temple robes.
          <br><br>
          The person begins a prayer. You have heard the first words before. You want to join in. A noise rises beneath them, like a laugh caught in a mouth full of water, and they lose the next word.
          <br><br>
          They try again. One of your parents says your name from beneath the bed. The person catches your sleeve as you step forward. A pale hand reaches past the doorway and closes where your ankle would have been.
          <br><br>
          <span class="red">The prayer has not stopped it.</span> The person draws you back to the stairs. Their free hand fumbles inside the robe, but they cannot find what they want.
          <br><br>
          "I can't do this alone." Their voice shakes. "Someone at the temple will know more than I do."
          <br><br>
          You ask if they are going away. They look at the open bedroom, then at you. "Come outside with me first." Behind them, the sheet rises without the brush touching it.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你指给那人看楼上的门，始终让楼梯留在自己身后。他蹲在卧室外，用刷子柄挑起床单。你还没来得及说别这样，黑暗里的苍白东西就转了过来。
          <br><br>
          对方喉咙里的呼吸停住了。他放下床单。“退后。”还没等有人碰到肩膀，你便照做了。
          <br><br>
          刷子滚进屋内。一根银色指甲钩住末端，木柄缓缓转动，直到指向神殿长袍的下摆。
          <br><br>
          那人开始祈祷。前几个字，你以前听过，你很想跟着一起念。另一阵动静却从下面升上来，像嘴里含着水的人在笑。他忘了下一个字。
          <br><br>
          他再试一次。床下，一位父母叫出你的名字。你往前迈，对方便捉住袖子。一只苍白的手越过门口，合拢在刚才你脚踝会在的位置。
          <br><br>
          <span class="red">祈祷没有让它停下。</span>那人拉着你退到楼梯边，另一只手慌乱地摸进长袍，却没找到想要的东西。
          <br><br>
          “我一个人做不了。”他的声音在抖，“神殿里总有人比我懂得多。”
          <br><br>
          你问他是不是要走了。他看看敞开的卧室，又看看你。“先跟我到外面。”他身后，刷子没有碰到床单，床单却自己抬起来了。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-private'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          The person sits with you on the outside step. The bag is between your shoes. They pull a loaf apart and give you a piece. You hold it without eating until they take a bite from their own.
          <br><br>
          "You can come with me." They name the temple. You look at the loaf, then up at the window.
          <br><br>
          "They'll know I've gone."
          <br><br>
          The person reaches for your hand and stops short of it. "I have to fetch someone." They pick up the bag. You tear a piece of bread off, smaller and smaller, until it has fallen between your shoes.
          <br><br>
          They write a name and the temple's address on a folded scrap. At the bottom they draw the turn beyond the shop. You make them point to the turn twice.
          <br><br>
          "Ask for me at the entrance. If they ask about your parents, tell them what you told me."
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('verdict-vow-sealed')>>Your mouth fills with the taste of the visitor's tea. You press your lips together. There is something you promised not to tell. The person waits for a reply, then says to keep the paper anyway.<<else>>You ask whether they will make you go under the bed to show them. The person shakes their head at once. Then they look away from the window. "I'll tell them what I saw."<</if>>
          <br><br>
          At the gate they turn and wave. You hold up the paper. The wind catches its corner. For a moment their shadow stays on the step beside you after they have gone. You move your shoe across it, and it slips away.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          那人在屋外的台阶上陪你坐下，袋子放在两双鞋之间。他掰开一条面包，递给你一块。你握着没有吃，直到他先咬了自己的那块一口。
          <br><br>
          “可以跟我一起走。”他说起神殿。你看看面包，再抬头看窗户。
          <br><br>
          “他们会知道我走了。”
          <br><br>
          那人伸手，停在快碰到你的地方。“我得去找个人。”他提起袋子。你撕下一小块面包，再撕小一点，直到它碎在两只鞋之间。
          <br><br>
          他拿一片折纸，写下名字和神殿的地址，在最下面画出商店后面该转的弯。你让他将那个转弯指了两遍。
          <br><br>
          “到入口找我。他们问起你的父母，就说刚才告诉我的那些。”
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('verdict-vow-sealed')>>嘴里涌上来客茶水的味道。你抿紧嘴唇。有些话，你已经答应不说。那人等着回答，最后还是让你把纸留好。<<else>>你问，他们会不会让你钻进床底，指给别人看。那人立刻摇头。随后，他不再望着窗户。“我会告诉他们，自己看见了什么。”<</if>>
          <br><br>
          走到大门，他转身挥手。你举起那张纸，风掀起一角。他已经走了，影子却还在你身旁的台阶上停了一会儿。你用鞋蹭过去，它才滑开。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-night-food'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You find a small scrap for your list. Bread. Water. You write too close to the edge, and the last word turns up the side. You tilt your head to check it. There ought to be something else, but you cannot decide whether it belongs on a list for tomorrow or in a question for an adult.
          <br><br>
          The folded paper with the name lies beside your cup. You read it twice, following the letters with a finger. You tuck your little list beneath it.
          <br><br>
          At supper you put your plate on the table. You lift another by habit, then leave it on the counter. You carry the food upstairs and leave it on the floor outside the bedroom now. You can set it down without crouching beside the gap, then return downstairs to the chair while your own food is still warm.
          <br><br>
          You sit where you can see the hall. A scrape comes from upstairs while you are chewing. You stop with the food in your mouth until it stops. Then you force yourself to swallow. Eating takes a long time this way. You move the folded paper farther from the cup so spilled water will not take the ordinary name away.
          <br><br>
          Your elbow knocks the cup. You catch it before it falls. For a moment you wait for the hand that would have caught it first. Yours is the only hand here. You find the coat button beneath your other wrist and press it once. It is still sewn on. You move that arm onto your lap before it can knock anything else.
          <br><br>
          It is not Sydney's cup. You can see that clearly now. You take another mouthful with your eyes on the doorway. Knowing which cup broke has not brought anybody back to the table. Outside, someone speaks beyond the gate. You cannot hear enough to know whether it is the person from earlier. You remain where the doorway is visible.
          <br><br>
          You finish the last piece. It has gone cold. There is still water, still a way to the garden, and still someone who has seen the window from outside. You wait for someone to ask whether you want more, then remember you can stand without permission. The chair makes a noise. The stairwell answers with another scrape.
          <br><br>
          You stand still until the scrape stops. At the sink you rinse the plate, turning off the tap between mouthfuls of water so you can listen. You resent how often you have to listen. The loaf is still on the counter. You cover it, then move the knife away from the edge. Your sleeve looks too small to be doing all of this, but the bread will dry if it is left out.
          <br><br>
          You carry the cup upstairs in one hand. On the landing, you use the other to keep the empty plate between yourself and the bedroom gap as you pass. A silver nail clicks against its underside. You nearly throw it, then hold on and take another step along the passage. The folded paper is in your pocket now. You keep that side of your coat away from the doorframe.
          <br><br>
          In your room you wish Sydney could see that you managed supper. Then you imagine <<nnpc_him 'Sydney'>> carrying a plate past that hand. You put your own plate down, then the cup. You check the door before finding a place for the two papers.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你找到一小片纸，准备写张清单。面包，水。字离边缘太近，最后那个词只好顺着纸边拐上去。你歪着头，确认自己还能读清。似乎还应该再写点什么，可你分不清，那件事究竟应该留在明天的清单上，还是留着问一个大人。
          <br><br>
          那张写着名字的折纸就放在杯子旁。你读了两遍，手指沿着字迹移动。你把小清单塞到它下面。
          <br><br>
          晚饭时，你把自己的盘子放到桌上。你习惯性地举起另一只，随后又留在柜台。现在，你把给父母的食物送上楼，放在卧室外的地上。你可以不用蹲在那道缝隙旁边，把东西搁下，再趁自己那份还没凉，下楼回到椅子上。
          <br><br>
          你挑了能看见大厅的位置坐。咀嚼到一半，楼上的刮擦又响起来。你把食物含在嘴里，等那个声音停了，才逼着自己吞下去。这样吃饭得花很久。你把折纸挪得离杯子远些，免得水洒出来，把那个普通的名字也泡坏。
          <br><br>
          手肘还是碰到了杯子。你赶在它掉下去之前抓住。有那么一瞬间，你还等着那只以前会先替你扶稳它的手。这里却只有你自己的手。另一边的手腕下面碰到外套扣子，你用指头压了一次，它还缝得好好的。你把那条胳膊挪到膝上，免得又碰到别的东西。
          <br><br>
          这只杯子不是悉尼的，现在你能看得很清楚。你又吃了一口，眼睛始终留意着门口。即使终于知道哪一只碎了，也没有人因此回到桌边。外面有人在大门附近说话，你听不清内容，不知道是不是先前的那个人。你仍留在能看见门口的位置。
          <br><br>
          最后一块终于吃完了。它已经凉透。家里仍然有水，仍然有一条去花园的路，也仍然有人从外面看见过破掉的窗户。你等了一会儿，等着谁问还要不要，随后记起，不必再得到允许也能够站起来。椅子挪动的声响刚停，楼梯间就用另一声刮擦回答。
          <br><br>
          你一动不动，直到它也停下。在水槽边，你洗了盘子，每喝一口水就把龙头关掉，听听外面的声音。你开始讨厌，自己怎么时时刻刻都得这样听。面包还在柜台上。你把它盖好，将刀挪到远离边缘的位置。做着这些事情的袖子看起来太小了，可要是不盖住，面包明天就会干掉。
          <br><br>
          你用一只手拿着杯子上楼。到了上层平台，经过父母门前时，另一只手把空盘子挡在自己和卧室缝隙之间。一根银色指甲敲到盘底。你差一点把它扔了，最后仍握紧，沿着过道继续迈出一步。现在，折纸已经在你的口袋里。你让外套的这一侧避开门框，没有挤过去。
          <br><br>
          到了房间，你很想让悉尼看见自己终于做好了晚饭。随后，你却想到，<<nnpc_him 'Sydney'>>也得拿着盘子经过那只手。你把自己的盘子放下，再放好杯子，先检查门，再为那两片纸找一块能够放好的地方。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-night-room'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          The cup is beside the bed. You check its water before turning away. You have carried it this far without losing all of it. The plate rests by the chair, where nobody has to lift a sheet to reach it.
          <br><br>
          You arrange the covers so your feet could get out quickly. You place the chair where you can reach it from the bed, then move it away from the door because you are afraid of being unable to open it yourself. You try the handle before lying down.
          <br><br>
          A knock comes from the passage, close to the floor. Two sounds, a pause, another. You sit up expecting Sydney. You remember where the bedroom is. The next knock comes from so low down that it seems to touch the underside of your mattress.
          <br><br>
          You put your feet back under the covers. You find the loose stitch. You listen for the stairs without calling any name. You have heard too many sounds answer the wrong things today. The folded paper is at the edge of your pillow. You move it where you could find it in the morning without reaching beneath the bed.
          <br><br>
          They told you to stay outside. You glance at your shoes and reach for one. A noise on the landing makes you let go. You grip the bedstead instead, watching the latch.
          <br><br>
          The edge of the lamplight has not reached the bed. You keep one finger hooked in the thread and wait for the knock to come again. The paper rustles beneath your pillow. You look at the cup once more before lying down.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          杯子就在床边。转头以前，你先看看里面的水。至少，拿到这么远，也没有把水全洒掉。盘子放在椅子旁，这里不会有谁得掀起一层被单，才能够到它。
          <br><br>
          你重新整理被子，好让两只脚能够迅速钻出去。椅子先被挪到从床边就能拿到的位置，随后又被你移开门口，因为你也怕自己会因此打不开门。准备躺下时，你先试了一遍把手。
          <br><br>
          过道里响起贴近地板的敲击声。先是两声，停顿以后，又是一声。你坐起来，一时以为会是悉尼。随后，你记起那间卧室究竟在哪里。下一次敲得太低了，仿佛直接碰到你的床垫底下。
          <br><br>
          你把双脚收回被子里，重新摸到那针松线。你听着楼梯，没有叫出任何人的名字。今天，已经有太多声音回答过不属于它们的东西。折纸放在枕头边缘，你把它移到早晨伸手就能找到的位置，不必再往床下摸。
          <br><br>
          那人让你待在外面。你看向自己的鞋，伸手去拿一只。楼梯间响起动静，你松了手，改为捉住床沿，盯着门闩。
          <br><br>
          灯光的边缘还没有到床边。你用一根手指勾着线，等那声敲击再次响起。纸在枕头下沙沙作响。躺下以前，你又看了一次杯子。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-morning'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You wake with the latch still in sight. The square of window light has moved off your knees. Your cup is where you left it, and nothing has pushed it over while you slept.
          <br><br>
          You sit up before remembering the house. For a moment you have an ordinary morning to waste: a sleeve to straighten, a shoe to find, a reason to stay in bed until somebody calls. Then you hear the low movement beneath the room and keep both feet on the mattress.
          <br><br>
          The paper with the adult's name has slipped beside your pillow. You find it by touch and unfold it. The ink has not become a drawing. You say the name quietly, then the turn in the street. You can still remember them. You do not know whether the person is coming today.
          <br><br>
          You want to look out first. You also want breakfast. The second want comes from your stomach and does not wait for the first to be answered. You fold the paper into your coat pocket, where it cannot drift under the bed, and lace your shoes.
          <br><br>
          In the upper passage, your parents' door stands as it did last night. You wait until you can hear the breath from below the bed, rather than somewhere along the boards. Then you pass it and reach the stairs, pausing where the rail is loose. The wood holds when you put your weight nearer the post. You use that part.
          <br><br>
          You go down to the kitchen. It smells of yesterday's bread. You eat a corner from the counter before taking the knife. A scrape sounds upstairs. You hold the loaf still until it stops.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你醒来时，还能看见门闩。窗户投下的那块方形光已经离开了你的膝盖。杯子仍在你留下的位置，没有什么趁你睡着，把它推倒。
          <br><br>
          你先坐起来，随后才想起这座房子。刚刚那一瞬间，仿佛本来是可以随便磨蹭的普通早晨：整理袖子，找一只鞋，想个理由继续待在床上，直到有人来叫。楼下却传来低低的动静，你立刻把两只脚都留在床垫上。
          <br><br>
          写着那个大人名字的纸滑到了枕头旁。你摸索着找到它，展开来，纸上的墨迹没有变成一幅画。你小声念了一遍名字，又念了一遍街上该转的弯。你仍然记得这些。你不知道，那个人今天会不会回来。
          <br><br>
          你想先看看外面，也想吃早餐。第二种想法从肚子里来，不肯等第一种得到回答。你把纸折好，放进外套口袋，免得它飘进床底，然后开始系鞋带。
          <br><br>
          上层过道里，父母的卧室门和昨晚一样半开着。你耐心等到自己能够听清，那口呼吸是在床底，而不是过道的某一块木板旁。随后，你经过房门，走到楼梯，在扶手松脱的地方停住。靠近柱子压下去时，那里的木头还撑得住，于是你只扶着那一段。
          <br><br>
          你下楼走进厨房，闻到昨天面包的味道。你从柜台上拿了一小角吃掉，再去拿刀。楼上响起刮擦。你握着面包不动，等它停下。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-breakfast'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>

          The old kitchen knife has a smooth dark wooden handle. You turn it until the blade faces away from your fingers, copying a movement you have watched many times. The first slice is too thick. The next breaks. You put the broken pieces on your own plate and feel briefly, fiercely annoyed with the bread.
          <br><br>
          Before the windows broke, your parent would have taken the knife and finished. You hold it still until that thought passes. Then you finish the third portion yourself and lay the blade flat, far from the counter's edge.
          <br><br>
          Three portions, a cup of water. You can make one trip if you balance everything. You can leave some behind and carry a single plate. <span class="blue">With only one hand occupied, you would still be able to move the chair or catch yourself.</span> You test the weight before lifting anything.
          <br><br>
          You check the spoon before filling the cup. A little bread is stuck to it. You rub it off with your thumb, scraping at the last stubborn crumb until a noise upstairs makes you stop.
          <br><br>
          Then you hear the bedroom again. You have finished cutting. It is time to decide how much your hands should hold on the next trip.
        <<option 'CN'>>

          旧菜刀的深色木柄很光滑。你转了转，让刀刃远离手指，学着看过很多次的动作。第一片太厚，下一片断了。你把碎的放进自己的盘子，一瞬间只觉得这条面包可恨。
          <br><br>
          窗户破掉以前，父母会接过刀，替你切完。你停住，等这个念头过去。随后，第三份也由你切好。你把刀平放，离柜台边缘很远。
          <br><br>
          三份食物，一杯水。全都端稳，一趟就能拿完。也可以留下一些，只拿一只盘子。<span class="blue">只占用一只手，还能挪椅子，或者在摔倒时撑住。</span>拿起之前，你先试了试分量。
          <br><br>
          给杯子装水以前，你看看勺子，上面粘着一点面包。你用拇指擦掉，又抠了抠最后那一点，楼上传来动静，你停了手。
          <br><br>
          随后，卧室里的动静又传来。面包已经切完，你得决定，下一趟要让自己的两只手拿多少东西。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-kitchen'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          The breathing is behind you.
          <br><br>
          You stop beside the table. You were listening towards the upstairs bedroom. Now the breath is at the kitchen door. Something has come down the stairs and moved across the part of the hall you could not see from the counter. Below the door's edge is a fold of black cloth, dragging over the floor. The smell reaches you before the pale fingers do.
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('breakfast-full')>>Both hands are full. You try to put everything down before it comes nearer, but the cup slides against a plate. Water strikes the floor. The black cloth moves at once. You let the plates fall onto the table, catch its edge with wet fingers, and pull your legs behind it. A silver nail catches the fallen cup instead of your ankle. You cannot pick the cup up.<<else>>You keep the plate close and seize the chair with your free hand. One leg catches under the table. You jerk it loose and put the chair between your knees and the doorway. Something presses against its back, hard enough to slide it. You put the plate down before bracing both arms against the table. The chair holds for another breath.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          "It's breakfast," you say.
          <br><br>
          For an instant you expect that to matter. The fingers close around empty air. You move sideways, never closer, until you can reach the garden door. Its handle is cold and ordinary. You get outside and keep hold of it until nothing follows.
          <br><br>
          You keep watching from outside. The food is still on the table, and there is enough bread for today. The cloth has not moved into the doorway. You need somewhere to stand where another person can see you, but the small shelf with the household coins is beside that door.
          <br><br>
          You stay outside long enough to see that the pale shape has not found the doorway. The chair and the cup do not return to their old places by themselves.
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('breakfast-full')>>You look at your wet hands. They had no room left for the table edge until everything fell.<<else>>You look at the chair. Its back still lies across the kitchen door. Something taps it from the other side.<</if>> You step off the sill before the black cloth moves again.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          呼吸声就在你身后。
          <br><br>
          你停在餐桌旁。你一直留意着楼上卧室的方向，现在那口呼吸却已经来到厨房门边。有什么下了楼梯，经过刚才从柜台上看不见的那段大厅。门沿下面，一折黑布拖着地板。苍白的手指还没有出现，你却已经闻到那股气味。
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('breakfast-full')>>你的两只手都拿满了东西。你想趁它还没靠近，把全部放下，杯子却先沿着盘子滑了一下。水洒在地板上，黑布立刻动了。你顾不上放稳，让盘子落到餐桌上，用湿透的手指抓住桌沿，将双腿收进桌子后面。一根银色指甲勾住了掉下去的杯子，没碰到你的脚踝。你却也再捡不回那只杯子。<<else>>你把盘子拿近身体，用空着的手抓住椅子。一条椅腿卡在桌下，你猛地把它扯开，挡在膝盖与门口之间。有什么压上椅背，力气大得让它往后滑。你赶紧放下盘子，用两条胳膊抵住餐桌。椅子又替你挡住了够喘一口气的时间。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          “是早餐。”你说。
          <br><br>
          有那么一瞬间，你以为这句话应该有用。那些手指却合拢在空处。你往侧面挪，始终没有靠近它，直到终于够到花园门。门把冰凉，仍然只是个普通的门把手。你走出去，一直握着它，等到确定没有什么跟来。
          <br><br>
          你继续从外面看。食物仍留在桌上，今天的面包暂时够了。那段布没有挪到门口。你需要一块站在那里就能被别人看见的地方，可放着家用零钱的小架子，偏偏也在这扇门旁。
          <br><br>
          你在外面待了一会儿，直到看清那个苍白的身影还没来到门口。椅子和杯子都没有自己回到原来的位置。
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('breakfast-full')>>你低头望着湿透的双手。直到手里的东西全掉下去以前，它们都没有空出来，能够抓住桌沿。<<else>>你看看那把椅子，椅背仍横在厨房门口。有什么从另一侧轻轻敲它。<</if>>你赶在黑布再次挪动以前，离开门槛。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-cup'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          Outside, you are still holding your hands as though there are plates on them. You lower one, then the other. The wet sleeve sticks to your wrist. You pull it free with your teeth because looking down for long feels unsafe.
          <br><br>
          The cup lies inside near the table leg. You can see the handle. It is not broken. You keep thinking that you should fetch it, although the distance between it and the doorway has not become any smaller.
          <br><br>
          You put one foot forward. Something shifts behind the table. You take the foot back. "Pick that up," you almost hear your parent say. You wait, but the words do not come. The cup stays on the floor.
          <br><br>
          When the sound moves away, you use the doorway to reach the small shelf beside it. The household coins are there. You take only the loose ones, leaving the container rather than letting it knock against the frame. Your fingers keep losing the smallest coin. You pick it up from the step where you can see both sides of your hand.
          <br><br>
          For a moment you think of the stranger's paper in your pocket. You cannot bring yourself to unfold it beside this open doorway. You can remember the shop. People stand there to buy things. You could stand there too, even if you do not have the right words for anything besides bread.
          <br><br>
          At the gate you stop and look back. The cup remains by the table. You rub your empty palm against your coat, push the coins deep into your pocket, and turn towards the shop.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          到了外面，你的两只手还维持着端盘子的样子。你先放下一只，再放下另一只。湿透的袖子贴在手腕上。你用牙咬住，把它稍稍拉开，因为一直低头看着手，似乎也会不安全。
          <br><br>
          杯子倒在屋里的桌腿附近。你看得见把手，它没有摔碎。你不断想着自己应该去捡，尽管杯子与门口之间的那段距离，始终没有变短。
          <br><br>
          你往前伸出一只脚，桌后有什么挪动，你又收回。“捡起来。”你几乎听见父母这样说。你等了一会儿，那句话却没有响起。杯子仍倒在地上。
          <br><br>
          那阵声音移开以后，你从门口伸手去够旁边的小架子。家里的零钱还在那里。你只拿了几枚散着的，没有带上盛它们的容器，免得容器碰响门框。最小的一枚不断从指间滑脱。你在台阶上捡起它，这里能看见自己的两只手，没有什么遮住。
          <br><br>
          有那么一瞬间，你想起口袋里那张陌生人留下的纸。可站在这个敞开的门口，你还不敢把它展开来，慢慢查看上面的字。不过，你仍记得商店在哪儿。人们会站在那里买东西，你也可以站在那里，哪怕除了面包之外，其他事情都还找不到合适的说法。
          <br><br>
          走到大门，你停下来回头看。杯子仍在桌边。你在外套上擦了擦空着的掌心，把硬币塞进口袋深处，转向商店。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-chair'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          The chair catches on the garden sill. You keep pulling until you are sure the black cloth has not reached the other side, then let it go. Its legs point into the kitchen. Your own legs are in daylight.
          <br><br>
          You sit on the step. You can feel where the chair struck one knee. The mark is small and ordinary. You rub around it instead of on it, and wait for your breath to stop sounding like a shout.
          <br><br>
          Inside, something moves the chair by one leg. You stand immediately. It stops. You cannot tell whether it is trying to get through or merely trying to move what you put there. You do not have to decide before stepping away.
          <br><br>
          For a while you stand near the wall and watch the gate. A cart passes. You lift a hand, but it has already turned the corner. You keep your hand up. Footsteps approach from the other end of the street.
          <br><br>
          You reach the little shelf from the doorway when the movement has gone back towards the stairs. There are household coins. You take a few, keeping one hand on the doorframe as you reach for the last. The chair scrapes inside. You snatch your hand back.
          <br><br>
          Before leaving, you move just far enough to see that the route from the step to the gate is clear. You do not inspect every window. You go along the path with both hands empty, and try the sentence you might say at the shop. The first word comes out. You try the next.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          椅子卡在通往花园的门槛上。你继续拉，直到确定那段黑布还没到门的这一侧，才放开手。椅腿朝着厨房。你自己的两条腿，已经到了日光里。
          <br><br>
          你坐上台阶，感觉到膝盖刚才被椅子撞过的位置。那个印子很小，只是普通的碰伤。你用手轻轻揉它周围，没有直接压上去，等着自己的呼吸不再响得像喊叫。
          <br><br>
          里面有什么碰着一条椅腿，开始挪动椅子。你立刻站起来。动静停了。你分不清它想挤过来，还是只想挪走你放在那里的东西。你不必先弄清，才能往旁边退开。
          <br><br>
          有一阵子，你贴着墙看大门。一辆车驶过，你抬手时，它已经转过街角。你没有放下手。街道另一头传来脚步声。
          <br><br>
          动静退回大厅、朝楼梯去了以后，你从门口够到小架子。家用零钱还放在那里。你拿了几枚，去够最后一枚时，另一只手仍捉着门框。屋里，椅子擦响地板。你猛地把手收回。
          <br><br>
          离开之前，你只走到能看清台阶通往大门的路的位置，没有逐一检查所有的窗户。你沿着小路往前，两只手都空着，试着练习自己在商店里可能会说的话。第一个字终于出了口，你又开始试下一个。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-shop'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          The corner shop smells of warm bread. You wait behind a woman arguing about the price, watching the shopkeeper's mouth move. Nobody whispers. Nobody stops when you look at them.
          <br><br>
          You put the coins down. One rolls over and shows a bright silver side. You press your thumb on it until the shopkeeper asks you to let go.
          <br><br>
          A bag is filled. In the glass behind the counter, a pale face looks over your shoulder. You turn. There is only another customer, reaching past you for a newspaper.
          <br><br>
          "Is someone coming for you?" the shopkeeper asks.
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('verdict-vow-sealed')>>You feel the cup from the visitor's table against your lips. You promised to keep something inside the house. The shopkeeper cannot see the cup. They wait, with a warm loaf in one hand, while your teeth close on the inside of your cheek.<<else>>You start to say yes. The shopkeeper looks at your shaking fingers. "Are you sure?" You pull yesterday's folded paper out of your pocket, then hide it beneath the bag again.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          Behind you, the customer turns the page. The noise is so much like paper tearing that you jump. The shopkeeper leaves the loaf on the counter and comes round to your side. "What's happened?"
        <<option 'CN'>>
          街角商店里闻得到热面包。你排在一个讨价还价的女人后面，看着店里人的嘴巴一张一合。没有谁在耳语，也没有谁因为你看过去，就突然停下。
          <br><br>
          你放下硬币。一枚翻过来，露出明亮的银色。你用拇指压住它，直到店里人让你松手。
          <br><br>
          袋子装好了。柜台后的玻璃里，一张苍白的脸从肩后望着你。你猛地转身，却只有另一位顾客越过你，伸手拿报纸。
          <br><br>
          “有人来接你吗？”店里的人问。
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('verdict-vow-sealed')>>来客桌上的杯子贴在你的嘴唇上。有些事，你答应过要留在屋里。店里的人看不见杯子。他一只手拿着热面包，等着你回答，你的牙齿却先咬住了脸颊内侧。<<else>>你差点说有。店里的人看看你发抖的手指。“真的？”你从口袋掏出昨天那张折纸，又藏回袋子下面。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          身后的顾客翻了一页报纸，响得太像撕纸声，你吓得一跳。店里的人将面包放到柜台上，绕到你这一侧。“出什么事了？”
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-help-home'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          "Something's wrong at home." You say it too loudly. The customer lowers the newspaper.
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-shop-break-silence')>>The visitor's voice snaps shut in your ear. "You promised." You bite your cheek hard enough to taste blood, then say the words again. The folded paper tears across the first letter of the name. You flatten both halves on the counter. <span class="red">You have broken the promise.</span> Three slow knocks sound from the glass.<<else>>The shopkeeper asks what you need. You point to the street, then the direction of home. "Come with me."<</if>>
          <br><br>
          They ask another customer to mind the counter and take off their apron. At the door you look behind them. The pale reflection is still in the glass, watching the two of you leave.
          <br><br>
          You walk close enough to catch their sleeve. At the manor gate, they see the windows and stop. You tell them someone from the temple came yesterday. They look at the name on the paper and read it twice.
          <br><br>
          "We'll ask at the temple. Stay out here with me."
          <br><br>
          You almost agree. A cup clicks from the kitchen. You had left it on the floor. The shopkeeper hears it too. They step between you and the garden door, call towards the street, and ask a passing person to fetch help.
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-shop-break-silence')>>Behind the glass, the visitor mouths your words in the wrong order. You turn your torn scrap over and write the street again. The shopkeeper's hand covers the corner to stop it blowing away.<<else>>You keep the scrap in your fist. The shopkeeper stays by the gate, taking one look towards the stairs each time you do.<</if>>
        <<option 'CN'>>
          “家里不对劲。”你说得太响了。顾客放低了报纸。
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-shop-break-silence')>>来客的声音猛地在耳边合拢。“你答应过。”你把脸颊咬出血味，随后又说了一遍。折纸沿着名字的第一个字裂开。你把两半都压在柜台上。<span class="red">你违背了承诺。</span>玻璃上传来三声缓慢的敲击。<<else>>店里的人问你需要什么。你指向街道，又指向家的方向。“跟我去。”<</if>>
          <br><br>
          他托另一位顾客看柜台，脱下围裙。到了门口，你回头望向他身后。苍白的倒影仍在玻璃里，看着你们两个离开。
          <br><br>
          你走得很近，伸手就能捉住他的袖子。到了庄园大门，对方看见窗户，停下了。你告诉他，昨天有个神殿里的人来过。他看着纸上的名字，读了两遍。
          <br><br>
          “我们去神殿问。你先跟我留在外面。”
          <br><br>
          你差点答应。厨房响了一下，是杯子碰到桌面的声音。你原本把它留在地上。店里的人也听见了，他站到你与花园门之间，朝街上喊，托一位路人去找帮手。
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-shop-break-silence')>>玻璃后面，来客的嘴唇动着，念出你刚说过的话，顺序却全不对。你翻过撕开的纸，再写一遍街道。店里的人用手压住一角，不让它吹走。<<else>>你把纸攥在手里。店里的人留在大门边，每次你望向楼梯，他就也望过去一次。<</if>>
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-alone-home'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          "Someone's waiting." The shopkeeper nods and puts a little more bread in the bag. You thank them twice. They have turned to the next customer before the second thank you is finished.
          <br><br>
          At the corner, you look back. The shop is still there. The person behind the counter lifts a loaf onto the scales. You grip the warm side of the bag and carry it home.
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('verdict-vow-sealed')>>At the gate a passer-by asks whether you are all right. You open your mouth. The visitor's cup touches your lips again. "Fine." The person walks on. As soon as they turn the corner, three slow knocks come from inside the manor.<<else>>At the gate a passer-by asks whether you are all right. You say you are waiting. They point at the broken window, but you duck your head. After a moment their footsteps move on.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          You put the bag on the low wall and sit beside it. The torn apron string you saw at the shop is caught in your mind. You wish you had grabbed it before the person went round the counter.
          <br><br>
          The paper is still in your pocket. You spread it on your knee. The name leads to the temple. The drawing at the bottom leads past the shop. You can follow it with your finger without taking a single step.
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('verdict-vow-sealed')>>The name is clear. Each time you try to say it, your mouth closes on the bloodless taste of tea. You fold the paper with the name inside.<<else>>You begin a message on the back and stop before finishing the first word. From behind the garden door, someone coughs exactly as your parent used to. You keep your pencil against the paper.<</if>>
        <<option 'CN'>>
          “有人在等。”店里的人点头，又往袋子里多放了一点面包。你道了两次谢，第二次还没说完，他已经转向下一位顾客。
          <br><br>
          街角，你回头看。商店还在那里，柜台后的人将一条面包搁上秤。你握着袋子温暖的那一侧，将它提回家。
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('verdict-vow-sealed')>>大门旁，一个路人问你还好不好。你张嘴，来客的杯子再次贴上嘴唇。“很好。”那人继续走。刚转过街角，庄园里便响起三声缓慢的敲击。<<else>>大门旁，一个路人问你还好不好。你说自己在等人。他指向破窗，你却低下头。过了一会儿，脚步声继续往前去了。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          你把袋子搁在矮墙上，坐到旁边。刚才在店里看见的那截破围裙带，一直留在脑袋里。你很想在那人绕回柜台前，先把它抓住。
          <br><br>
          纸还在口袋里。你将它摊在膝上，名字通往神殿，最下面的图经过商店。你用手指跟着走，自己一步也没迈。
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('verdict-vow-sealed')>>名字很清楚。每次想念出来，嘴里却只有冷茶水的味道。你折起纸，把名字留在里面。<<else>>你开始往纸背写消息，第一个字还没写完就停住。花园门后，有人像父母从前那样咳了一声。你没有把铅笔从纸上移开。<</if>>
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-late'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          <<if !$LostLamb.marks.includes('window-checked') and !$LostLamb.marks.includes('contact-left') and !$LostLamb.marks.includes('rest-space')>>You put the bag beside the garden wall. The paper blows off your knee. You catch it against the stones before the wind can take it towards the open door.<<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('brought-help') or $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-shop-break-silence')>> The shopkeeper calls from the gate. You hold up one finger. They stop, though you meant one more minute, not silence.<</if>><</if>>
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('window-checked')>>Through the kitchen window you can see the gate. You keep your head below the upstairs window and shift along the wall until its dark square is hidden.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('contact-left')>>The writing is pinned beneath the bag. From the street someone can read where you mean to wait. From the house a shadow creeps across the first line. You move the bag a little farther into the light.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('rest-space')>>Your legs will take your weight again. You stand with a hand on the wall and lift the bag. The bread is cold now, but the handle has not broken.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('contact-left')>>The garden door knocks against its frame. <span class="blue">Your things are still close enough to fetch before the light moves.</span><<elseif $LostLamb.marks.includes('verdict-vow-sealed')>>The temple's address lies across your palm. You remember the visitor's cup touching your lips. From the house, the voice says, "Good <<pcGender>>." You turn the paper over. There is room for a message on the back.<<else>>You stare at the temple's address. The person who wrote it does not know where you are sitting now. You turn the paper over and start with the gate.<</if>>
        <<option 'CN'>>
          <<if !$LostLamb.marks.includes('window-checked') and !$LostLamb.marks.includes('contact-left') and !$LostLamb.marks.includes('rest-space')>>你把袋子放到花园墙边。纸从膝上吹走，你赶在风将它送向敞开的门以前，把它按到石头上。<<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('brought-help') or $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-shop-break-silence')>> 店里的人在大门旁喊，你举起一根手指。他便停了。可你想说的是再等一分钟，不是别出声。<</if>><</if>>
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('window-checked')>>透过厨房窗户，你看得见大门。你压低头，沿墙挪动，直到楼上那块黑色窗框被挡住。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('contact-left')>>新写的字压在袋子下面。街上的人能读到你在哪里等。房子这边，一道影子爬上第一行。你将袋子挪向更亮一点的位置。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('rest-space')>>腿又能够站稳了。你一只手扶墙，站起来提袋子。面包已经冷了，把手却没有断。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('contact-left')>>花园门撞了一下门框。<span class="blue">日光还没移开，东西仍近得能够去拿。</span><<elseif $LostLamb.marks.includes('verdict-vow-sealed')>>神殿的地址横在掌心上。你记得来客的杯子贴到嘴唇。屋里的声音说：“好<<pcGender>>。”你翻过纸，背面还有地方能写消息。<<else>>你盯着神殿的地址。写下它的人，还不知道你正坐在哪里。你翻过纸，先写大门。<</if>>
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-window'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You step just inside the kitchen and stand to one side of its garden-facing window. From here the glass reflects only a little of your face. The gate is beyond it, open far enough for an ordinary person to pass through.
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('brought-help') or $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-shop-break-silence')>>The shopkeeper turns towards somebody outside. You cannot hear the words. They point once towards the house, then lower their arm when they see you watching. You know they have been talking about what they saw. You do not know what name they used for it.<<else>>The person who stopped on the pavement remains near the gate. They ask somebody passing which way the address on your paper is. You can see the other person point. There is a turn beyond the shop you would not have remembered on your own.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          You want to open the window and listen. The catch sticks. Before you can pull harder, you hear something from the upstairs bedroom through the stairwell behind you. You let the catch go. From this angle you can see outside without letting every noise outside into the room.
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('flower')>>A dry petal lies near the sill. You think of the flower you gave Sydney and look for the rest. There is no flower here, only a bit of leaf that the wind has pressed flat. You leave it alone.<<else>>A bit of leaf lies near the sill. You cannot remember whether it arrived today. You brush it aside with one finger, watching it move like an ordinary leaf.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          The person at the gate looks up. You raise your hand. They answer, then turn towards someone you cannot see. A second hand draws the raised arm down. You press your fingers to the glass and wait for it to lift again.
          <br><br>
          Inside, the breathing changes. Outside, the conversation continues. You move away from the window and back outside through the garden doorway before the first sound can make you forget there is a second.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你刚踏进厨房，便站到朝向花园的窗户一侧。从这里，玻璃只映出你脸上的一小部分。再往外就是大门，开着的空隙够一个普通人从中间走过。
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('brought-help') or $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-shop-break-silence')>>店里的人转身，和外面的一个人说话。你听不见他们说什么，只看见他往房子这里指了一次。发现你在看，他又把手臂放低。你知道，他们正在谈论看见的东西，却不知道他们会用什么名字称呼它。<<else>>那位在人行道上停下的人仍在大门旁。他问了一个路过的人，纸上的地址应该怎么走。你看见那个人抬手指路。原来商店过去还得再转一个弯，只靠自己，你不会记起那段路。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          你想打开窗户，听清他们的话。窗扣卡住了。你还没敢更用力，楼上卧室的动静就顺着身后的楼梯间传下来。你松开窗扣。从这个角度，仍然能够看见外面，不必把外面的每一种声音都放进屋里。
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('flower')>>窗台边躺着一片干枯的花瓣。你想起给过悉尼的那朵花，低头寻找剩下的部分。这里却没有一朵花，只有一小片被风压平的叶子。你没有碰它。<<else>>窗台旁有一小片叶子。你记不清，它是今天才到这里的，还是已经待了很久。你用一根手指把它拨到旁边，看它像一片普通的叶子那样挪动。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          大门旁的人抬起头。你举手，他也抬手回应，随后转向一个你看不见的人。第二只手把举起的胳膊拉下。你用手指压着玻璃，等着它再举起来。
          <br><br>
          里面的呼吸变了，外面的谈话却还在继续。你赶在前一种声音让自己忘记还有后一种之前，从窗户旁退开，经过花园门回到外面。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-message'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You turn the paper over. "At the garden gate." You write the street underneath, then that the bedroom is dangerous. The pencil slips from your fingers. You pick it up and finish the last word.
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-message-break-silence')>>The paper folds over your knuckles by itself. The visitor's voice says the promise you made, one word for each crease. You pull it flat. The last fold splits, taking part of the old name with it. <span class="red">You write over the tear.</span> When you look up, the garden door is open wider than before.<<elseif $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-shop-break-silence')>>There is already a tear through the name. You hold its edges together and write beneath them. The visitor's voice is waiting behind the garden door. You do not turn towards it.<<else>>A sound comes from upstairs. You press too hard and snap the pencil point. You use the broken edge to finish the address, leaving a thick, ugly mark.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('brought-help') or $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-shop-break-silence')>>You show the shopkeeper. They read it, then call the place back towards the house so the person coming from the temple will hear. You catch their sleeve and ask them not to go in. They look past you and leave their feet where they are.<<else>>You stand at the gate with the message held up. A passer-by slows down. You have to call twice before they stop. You show them the name and say the temple's address. They read the scrap, look at the windows, and ask you to stay where you can be seen.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          "Don't close the gate," they say.
          <br><br>
          You press the paper beneath the bag with the new writing showing. Through the gap in the garden doorway, you see a silver nail resting where the latch should be. It withdraws when the person outside says they will send someone.
          <br><br>
          You ask how soon. There is no answer you can count to. The person names the temple again and points down the street. You hold the gate open until they have gone beyond the corner.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你翻过那张纸。“在花园大门。”下面写街道，再写卧室有危险。铅笔从指间滑出去。你捡起来，将最后一个字写完。
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-message-break-silence')>>纸自己折起来，裹住指节。来客的声音念着你作过的承诺，每道折痕一个字。你把纸拉平。最后一折裂开，带走旧名字的一部分。<span class="red">你越过裂口，继续写。</span>抬头时，花园门比刚才开得更大。<<elseif $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-shop-break-silence')>>名字中间已经有了一道裂口。你把两边压在一起，在下面写字。来客的声音等在花园门后，你没有转过去。<<else>>楼上传来动静。你用力太重，铅笔尖断了。你就用断口将地址写完，留下一块又粗又丑的痕迹。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('brought-help') or $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-shop-break-silence')>>你将纸给店里的人看。他读完，朝房子那边重复了地点，好让从神殿来的人听见。你抓住袖子，求他别进去。他越过你往里看，两只脚却留在原处。<<else>>你站在大门旁，举着消息。一位路人慢下来。你喊了两次，他才停下。你给他看名字，说出神殿的地址。他读了纸条，看看窗户，让你待在看得见的地方。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          “别关大门。”对方说。
          <br><br>
          你用袋子压住那张纸，让新写的字露在外面。隔着花园门的缝隙，你看见一根银色指甲停在本该有门闩的位置。外面的人说会叫人来，它便缩走了。
          <br><br>
          你问还要多久。没有一个答案能够靠数数等完。那人再次说起神殿，向街道指去。你一直把大门撑开，直到对方走过街角。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-rest'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You drag the bag off the step and sit with your back to the wall. You make yourself untie the loose lace. It takes three tries to get the ends through the knot.
          <br><br>
          A little insect crosses your shoe. You jerk your foot and knock the bag. Bread falls onto the grass. You snatch it up before anything can crawl over it, brushing dirt away with your sleeve.
          <br><br>
          You are angry at the bread, at the bag, at the people who keep saying they need someone else. You are angry at Sydney. You start to say that <<nnpc_he 'Sydney'>> should have come anyway.
          <br><br>
          Two knocks sound from the house. You bite back the name before the third. Beneath the broken window, a short pencil rolls out of the shadow and stops against your shoe.
          <br><br>
          You pull your foot away. The pencil stays where it is. You put the bread back in the bag and knot your lace, badly, with both hands. Your legs have steadied enough to stand.
          <br><br>
          The sunlight reaches the next few steps. You keep the wall against your shoulder and leave the pencil on the ground.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你把袋子拖出台阶，背靠墙坐下，逼自己解开那根松鞋带。试了三次，才让两头从结里面穿出来。
          <br><br>
          一只小虫爬过鞋面。你猛地收脚，撞到袋子，面包滚上草。你赶在有什么爬上去以前捡起来，用袖子拍掉泥土。
          <br><br>
          你生面包的气，生袋子的气，也生那些总说还得找别人的人的气。你生悉尼的气。你开始说，<<nnpc_he 'Sydney'>>不管怎样，都该来的。
          <br><br>
          屋里敲了两下。第三下以前，你咬住了没说完的名字。破窗下面，一支短铅笔滚出阴影，停在鞋边。
          <br><br>
          你把脚抽走，铅笔却留在原处。你将面包塞回袋子，两只手一起把鞋带系成一个难看的结。腿已经不抖得那么厉害，能够站了。
          <br><br>
          日光还照着接下来的几步。你沿着墙走，将铅笔留在地上。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-attempt'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You mean to move only the things beside the garden door. The bag is there, and a cup you can use outside. From the wall, the doorway looks close enough that you have already made the trip in your head.
          <br><br>
          You lift the bag first. Then you see the chair. It is not where you left it. One broken leg lies across the space that was clear. You put the bag down before trying to get past it.
          <br><br>
          The kitchen threshold is dark. Something in black cloth is between it and the stairs, lower than a person would be if they stood to speak to you. You cannot see whether the pale shoulder belongs to the thing from the morning or the other parent. You cannot see the upstairs bedroom door from here at all.
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('kept-silence')>>You hear yesterday's young temple voice from the garden. "They've agreed. Come inside." You turn to follow it. The garden gate is empty. The next word sounds from the kitchen, on the other side of the pale shoulder. You snatch your foot back.<<elseif $LostLamb.marks.includes('brought-help') or $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-shop-break-silence')>>You call to the shopkeeper by the gate. They come along the path, telling you to step back outside. For a moment you have a voice to follow. Then the pale shape moves across the entrance. The adult catches the door before it can strike you, and the noise makes the black cloth shift towards both of you. "Up," they say, seeing the stairs beyond it. "I'll stay here. Go up."<<else>>You turn towards the garden. The bag tips against the frame behind your heel. The pale shape moves at the sound. You have room to step back, but not room to turn without bringing your shoulder near it. You hear the person at the gate calling to ask what happened. Your voice will not reach them before the next movement.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          You leave the bag. The table is beside the garden doorway. A small tin sits near its edge, and the door beyond is open. On the other side of the hall a narrow strip runs against the wall towards the stairs. You look at both without moving your feet.
          <br><br>
          <span class="red">Yesterday's safe place is occupied. The window light ends before the staircase.</span> You can make a sound somewhere you do not intend to stand. You can try to get through the quiet strip before anything turns back towards you.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你本来只想挪动花园门旁的几样东西。袋子还在那里，旁边也有一只可以拿到外面用的杯子。从墙边望过去，门口近得很，仿佛你已经在脑海里来回走过了一趟。
          <br><br>
          你先提起袋子，随后才看见那把椅子。它没有停在你留下的位置。一条折断的椅腿横在曾经空出来的路上。你把袋子放下，才试着从旁边经过。
          <br><br>
          厨房门槛很暗。裹在黑布里的东西停在门槛和楼梯之间，比一个站起来跟你说话的人低得多。你看不清，那块苍白的肩膀属于早晨的那一个，还是另一位父母。从这里，你甚至看不见楼上卧室的门。
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('kept-silence')>>昨天那个年轻的神殿声音从花园里传来。“他们答应了。到里面来。”你转身想跟过去，大门边却空着。下一个字从厨房里响起，在苍白肩膀的另一侧。你猛地将脚收回。<<elseif $LostLamb.marks.includes('brought-help') or $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-shop-break-silence')>>你朝大门旁的店里人喊了一声。他沿着小路过来，让你退回外面。有那么一瞬间，你有了一个能够跟随的声音。随后，那块苍白的影子移过入口。他赶在门撞上你之前接住门，发出的响声却让黑布转向了你们两个人。“上去。”他看见它后面的楼梯，“我留在这里。往楼上走。”<<else>>你转向花园。袋子在脚跟后面倾倒，碰响了门框。苍白的影子循着响声挪动。你还能够后退，却没办法转身，除非把肩膀带到离它更近的地方。大门旁的人正在喊，问你发生了什么。你知道，在下一次移动之前，自己的声音已经来不及传到那边。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          你把袋子留在原地。桌子靠着通向花园的门，一个小罐放在桌沿，更外面的门还开着。大厅另一边，一条窄窄的地方贴墙通向楼梯。你看着这两个方向，没有挪动自己的脚。
          <br><br>
          <span class="red">昨天能够站稳的位置已经被占住。窗户投下的光还没有到楼梯，就断开了。</span>你可以让某个声音出现在自己不打算停留的地方。你也可以试着趁它还没转回来，从那条安静的窄路挤过去。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-noise-way'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You knock the tin towards the open garden door. It strikes the sill, bounces, and rolls outside. The cloth shifts after it. You run the other way. For a moment the room gives you the space you expected. Then a pale arm catches the banister above your head. You crouch before you know you have crouched and scramble beneath it. Your shoulder hits a stair. The tin is still rolling when you find the first stair.
          <br><br>
          A strip of cloth catches on the stair edge below you. You pull your own shirt up before it can brush that cloth. The tin strikes something in the garden and stops. You wish it would keep rolling.
          <br><br>
          The thing beneath you turns back. You hear weight press against the first step, then the wood give a small complaint. You go up the next two without waiting to hear the next. Your breath is louder than your feet now. You stop trying to make both quiet.
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('kept-silence')>>The young voice says the stairs are safe. It comes from below your feet. You hold the rail tighter and keep climbing. The pale hand follows where the voice said to step.<<elseif $LostLamb.marks.includes('brought-help') or $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-shop-break-silence')>>The adult at the entrance shouts towards the garden, drawing another movement away from your legs. You cannot see them from here. You grip the rail and keep climbing.<<else>>The person outside calls again. You want to answer, but the breath needed for the next stair uses the whole word. You take the stair. There will be another place to speak if you reach the landing.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('shortcut')>>You reach the turn and duck through before the thing below can follow, with the same quick movement that won the garden race. This time you do not stop to claim the win.<<elseif $LostLamb.marks.includes('waited')>>At the turn you almost wait for the person behind you, as you waited in the garden. You force your legs on. There is no friend to catch up.<<else>>You go up the narrow side of the stairs, keeping the wider part between yourself and the sound behind you.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          You find the rail's firm part by the post. You put your hand there, take the last step of the turn, and look towards the room that is still your room.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你把小罐扫向开着的花园门。它撞上门槛，弹一下，滚到外面。黑布跟着动，你朝另一边跑。有一瞬，屋里果然空出了预想的位置。随后，一条苍白手臂抓上头顶的扶手。你还没想，就已经蹲下，从下面往上爬。肩膀撞到一级楼梯。你找到第一级台阶时，小罐还在滚。
          <br><br>
          下面的楼梯边缘勾住了一段布。你赶紧提起自己的上衣，不让衣角擦到它。扔到花园里的小罐撞上什么，终于停了下来。你很希望它还能继续滚，别这么快安静。
          <br><br>
          下面那个东西又转回来。你听见重量压上第一级台阶，木头发出一声细响。你不等下一声，就继续爬了两级。自己的呼吸已经比脚步响，你没有再试着让两种声音都安静。
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('kept-silence')>>年轻的声音说，楼梯很安全。声音来自脚下。你更紧地捉住扶手，继续爬。苍白的手追上了刚才它让你落脚的位置。<<elseif $LostLamb.marks.includes('brought-help') or $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-shop-break-silence')>>入口的大人朝花园喊了一声，把另一阵动静从你的腿旁引开。你在这里看不见他，便握紧扶手，继续往上爬。<<else>>外面的人又在叫你。你想回答，下一阶却已经用掉了一整口气，连一个字也放不进去。你先把那级台阶踩上去。如果能到楼梯间，就还会有别的地方让你开口。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('shortcut')>>到了转弯，你用赢过花园比赛的同一个急转身钻过去，没让下面的东西跟上。这次，你没停下来宣布自己赢了。<<elseif $LostLamb.marks.includes('waited')>>转弯时，你差点像在花园里那样，等身后的人。你逼着腿继续。没有朋友要追上来。<<else>>你沿楼梯窄的一侧上去，让更宽的那半边隔在自己和后面的动静之间。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          你找到靠柱子那段结实的扶手，把掌心放稳，迈过转角的最后一级台阶。那间仍然属于你的房间，就在前面。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-wall-way'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You press yourself against the wall and move towards the stairs. You try not to brush the paper peeling near the skirting. Halfway there, the wall seems to end. A pale shoulder is beside it, low enough to be yours if you bent down. You stop. It moves when the bag falls sideways behind you. You slip past before it turns back, keeping your stomach pulled tight so your shirt will not touch it.
          <br><br>
          The peeling paper brushes your ear. You nearly swat at it. Instead you hold your arm close, where an ordinary movement will not strike the wall. The pale shoulder turns below you.
          <br><br>
          You have found the stairs, but the first board is the one that sounds loudest. You place a foot nearer its edge. The other foot comes up before you have decided whether it made too much noise. If you go back to check, you will be in the hall again.
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('kept-silence')>>"This way." The temple voice calls from the hall behind you. You turn your head and see a silver nail tapping the lowest stair. You crawl up the next step without answering.<<elseif $LostLamb.marks.includes('brought-help') or $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-shop-break-silence')>>The adult at the entrance says to keep going. Their voice cracks. You grip the rail and climb another step. They call again before you reach the turn.<<else>>A voice outside asks where you are. You manage to say "upstairs", too quietly. You say it again at the turn. Your foot catches the stair lip while you speak, and you grip the post until it stops sliding.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('shortcut')>>You reach the turn and duck through before the thing below can follow, with the same quick movement that won the garden race. This time you do not stop to claim the win.<<elseif $LostLamb.marks.includes('waited')>>At the turn you almost wait for the person behind you, as you waited in the garden. You force your legs on. There is no friend to catch up.<<else>>You go up the narrow side of the stairs, keeping the wider part between yourself and the sound behind you.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          You no longer know whether the whole route behind you is clear. You know the next stair is clear because you can see it. You take that one, keeping your body close to the rail where a reaching hand would have less room.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你贴墙，往楼梯走，尽量不蹭到踢脚板旁翘起的墙纸。走到一半，墙像是到头了。旁边有一只苍白肩膀，低得你弯腰也会在那里。你停住。身后，袋子倒向一边，它循声动了。你赶在它转回来之前挤过，收紧肚子，不让上衣碰上。
          <br><br>
          翘起的墙纸擦到你的耳朵，你差一点抬手拍掉。最后，你只把手臂贴紧身体，没有让这个普通的动作敲响墙面。下面那块苍白的肩膀转动了。
          <br><br>
          你找到楼梯，第一块木板却偏偏是平时最响的那一块。你把脚放到更靠边的位置，还没想好刚才的声音会不会太大，另一只脚就已经抬了上来。假如回去检查，你就又得站到大厅里。
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('kept-silence')>>“这边。”神殿的声音在身后的大厅叫。你转头，一根银色指甲正敲着最下面一级楼梯。你没有回答，先爬上下一阶。<<elseif $LostLamb.marks.includes('brought-help') or $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-shop-break-silence')>>入口的大人让你继续走，声音却破了。你握紧扶手，再爬一级。还没到转角，他又喊了一声。<<else>>外面的声音问你在哪。你勉强说出“楼上”，却太轻了。到了转角，你又说了一次。讲话的时候，脚尖勾住台阶边缘，你赶紧握紧柱子，等脚终于不再往下滑。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('shortcut')>>到了转弯，你用赢过花园比赛的同一个急转身钻过去，没让下面的东西跟上。这次，你没停下来宣布自己赢了。<<elseif $LostLamb.marks.includes('waited')>>转弯时，你差点像在花园里那样，等身后的人。你逼着腿继续。没有朋友要追上来。<<else>>你沿楼梯窄的一侧上去，让更宽的那半边隔在自己和后面的动静之间。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          你不知道身后整条路是不是仍然空着。可下一阶就在眼前，能够看清，所以至少知道那里还能踩。你迈上去，让身体贴近扶手，尽量不在身旁留出一只手能够伸过来的空隙。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-upstairs'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          The landing is bright enough to make you blink. You had expected the dark to be waiting at the top as well. The window is still a window, with dust at its edge and a little crack you have seen before.
          <br><br>
          You stop for the smallest part of a breath. Below, the stair sounds again. You move before you can count how many steps have been taken. Your own door is ahead. The handle is at the height your hand expects.
          <br><br>
          You get inside and push. The door stops. For one instant you know that it has found the same wrong place as the doors in the other dreams. Then you look down. <span class="blue">The rug is bunched at the threshold.</span>
          <br><br>
          You could keep pushing. Your shoulder already wants to. It would make more noise and keep the rug there. You plant your shoe on one corner and pull it backwards. The fabric moves. You push again, and the opening grows smaller.
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('kept-silence')>>The voice says it has brought help. You look past the rug. There is no pair of shoes beyond the door. Black cloth lies against the lower panel and something beneath it draws a breath to speak again.<<elseif $LostLamb.marks.includes('brought-help') or $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-shop-break-silence')>>The person below calls that they are still at the entrance. You cannot see whether they are looking up. You say "here" while holding the door, giving them a place rather than trying to explain the movement on the stairs.<<else>>The voice outside calls your name. You say "here", then louder, "upstairs". The second word uses a breath you were trying to save. You are glad you used it when the voice answers.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          The edge of the rug is nearly out of the opening. You need to pull it a little farther while keeping the door from springing back. Your shoe begins to slip. You set your palm flat against the wood, trying to leave the fabric where it cannot keep the latch from catching.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          楼梯间亮得让你眨了眨眼。你原本以为，那片黑暗也会在楼梯顶端等着。窗户却仍是一扇窗，边缘积着灰，玻璃上有一道你以前就见过的小裂纹。
          <br><br>
          你只能停下不到一口气。下面的楼梯再次响了。还没来得及数，到底已经被踩过几阶，你就继续往前。自己的房门在前面，门把手仍留在你伸手时所记得的高度。
          <br><br>
          你钻进去，推门。门停住了。有那么一瞬间，你觉得它也停在另外两个梦里那些门停错的位置。随后，你低头看见，<span class="blue">地毯挤在了门槛上。</span>
          <br><br>
          你还可以继续推，肩膀已经想那样做了。可那只会让声音更响，也让地毯继续留在那里。你把鞋踩住地毯的一角，试着往后拖。布挪动了一点。你再推，门口的空隙终于缩小。
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('kept-silence')>>那个声音说，带来了帮手。你越过地毯看，门外没有一双鞋。黑布贴在下面的门板上，布底的东西吸进一口气，准备再次说话。<<elseif $LostLamb.marks.includes('brought-help') or $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-shop-break-silence')>>楼下的人喊，他仍在入口。你看不见他有没有抬头。你一边抵门，一边回答“这里”，先给他一个位置，不试着解释楼梯上的那阵动静。<<else>>外面的人正在叫你的名字。你先说“这里”，随后更大声地说“楼上”。第二句话用掉了你本来想省下的一口气。不过，等那个声音答应时，你又庆幸自己用了。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          地毯边沿几乎已经挪出门口。你还得再把它拉开一点，同时让门别弹回来。鞋底开始打滑。你把掌心平贴在门上，试着让那块布留在不会挡住门闩的位置。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-latch'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          The metal tongue catches. You feel it through the wood before taking your palm away. <span class="green">The door stays shut.</span>
          <br><br>
          Something touches the lower panel, pauses, and moves along the skirting. You press your ear to the frame. It stops moving. You draw back, holding your breath.
          <br><br>
          You put the chair against the door, then stare at its legs. If you leave it there, you cannot open the door either. You drag it back beside the bed. It scrapes loudly. The noise outside stops.
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('kept-silence')>>The temple robes are in the window. You hurry to the glass. The gate outside is empty. The robes are a reflection, on your side of the pane. You spin round. There is only your closed door. "We've agreed," the voice whispers through the keyhole.<<else>>A voice below the window calls your name. You go to the glass. Yesterday's temple robes are visible by the gate, beside someone taller. The younger one raises a hand. The other catches their wrist before they can move towards the entrance.
          <br><br>
          You shout which room you are in. The hand is lifted again. You press your fingers against the glass and wait for the next question.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          Behind you, a nail taps the latch from the wrong side. You turn, but the small metal tongue is still in its slot.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          金属舌扣进去了。你隔着木头感觉到那一下，才挪开掌心。<span class="green">门仍然关着。</span>
          <br><br>
          有什么碰到下面的门板，停住，又沿着踢脚板移动。你把耳朵贴在门框上，动静也停了。你屏住呼吸，将脸移开。
          <br><br>
          你将椅子抵在门上，随后盯着椅腿。要是留在那里，你也打不开门。你把它拖回床旁，刮得很响。门外的动静停了。
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('kept-silence')>>神殿长袍出现在窗上。你赶到玻璃边，外面的大门却空着。长袍是倒影，在窗户的你这一侧。你猛地转身，只有自己紧闭的门。“我们答应了。”那个声音透过锁眼低语。<<else>>窗下有人叫你的名字。你走到玻璃旁。大门边，昨天那件神殿长袍站在另一个更高的人身旁。年轻的那个抬起手，想朝入口走，另一个却先捉住了他的手腕。
          <br><br>
          你喊出自己在哪个房间。那只手再次举起来。你用手指压着玻璃，等着下一个问题。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          身后，一根指甲从不该碰到的那一侧敲响门闩。你转身，小小的金属舌却仍扣在槽里。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-brace'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You pull before your foot is clear. The rug folds over itself instead of sliding out. The door strikes its thick edge and rebounds. <span class="red">Your fingers miss the latch.</span>
          <br><br>
          A weight meets the other side. You throw your shoulder against the wood. The opening is wider than a finger, narrow enough that you cannot see what is pressing there. A strip of black cloth reaches it first. You stare at that strip, forgetting the rug until the door moves another little distance.
          <br><br>
          You need the corner beneath your foot, not the whole rug at once. You put your heel on it. Your shoe slips. You turn the shoe sideways and catch the fabric against its edge, keeping your shoulder where the other weight is pushing.
          <br><br>
          Below you, the folded part moves. You draw it back a little, stop when the pressure changes, and draw it again. Your ankle aches before the door has enough room. When the thick edge starts coming clear, the latch is suddenly near your fingers.
          <br><br>
          You cannot reach the metal and hold the door steady with the same hand. You keep the shoulder there instead. Your knee is against the rug. You try not to push that down as well, and trap the very corner you have been trying to free.
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('kept-silence')>>The voice behind the door asks whether you are hurt. It says it can mend your foot if you move aside. You press your shoulder harder against the wood. The black cloth wriggles towards the ankle it has just named.<<else>>Outside, an ordinary person has heard the noise. They ask whether you are hurt. You say your foot hurts. When they ask which window belongs to your room, you answer without taking your shoulder away. The weight on the other side changes, then returns.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          You leave the wardrobe where it is. You cannot move all of it now. The corner of cloth can come towards your heel if you pull it a little farther. You watch that corner, keeping your body against the place that wants to open.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          脚还没有让开，你就开始拉了。地毯没滑出去，反而折叠起来。门撞上那条厚厚的边，又弹回你这边。<span class="red">你的手指错过了门闩。</span>
          <br><br>
          另一侧压来一股重量。你猛地用肩膀顶住木头。门口的缝比一根手指宽，却又窄得看不清，究竟是什么正压在那里。先挤进来的是一段黑布。你盯住它，一时忘了脚下的地毯，直到门又被推开一点。
          <br><br>
          你需要挪的是脚下那个角，不是一下拖走整张地毯。你把脚跟压上去，鞋却滑开了。你重新把鞋转向侧面，用鞋边勾住布，肩膀仍顶在另一侧的重量压来的地方。
          <br><br>
          折起来的那部分终于动了。你往后拖一点，门上的压力改变时就停住，随后再拖。门还没有足够合拢的位置，脚踝已经开始酸疼。厚边终于开始让开时，门闩忽然又到了手指能够到的地方。
          <br><br>
          你没办法用同一只手，既去够金属，又把门稳住。你只好继续让肩膀顶在那里。膝盖还压着地毯，你努力别让它也跟着用力，重新卡住那个好不容易才拖出来的角。
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('kept-silence')>>门后的声音问你是不是受伤了，说只要让开，就能治好你的脚。你用肩膀更紧地顶住木头。黑布扭向它刚才提过的脚踝。<<else>>外面有个普通人听见了响声，问你有没有受伤。你说脚疼。他又问，哪一扇窗属于你的房间。你回答时没有移开肩膀。另一侧的重量变了一下，随后又压回来。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          你没有试着去够衣柜，现在也搬不动它。只要再多拉一点，那块布的角就能够到脚跟下面。你盯着那个角，仍用自己的身体抵住这扇正想打开的门。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-inbed'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          You try the latch once more, then pull your fingers away. Your knees ache where they have pressed against the rug. You rub one, with your eyes on the gap below the door.
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('rest-space')>>You stretch one leg as you did on the step, then use the bedpost to stand. The badly tied lace drags over the rug. You step clear of it before moving the other foot.<<else>>You stand too quickly. Your numb foot folds beneath you. You sit down hard, grip the bedpost, and get up with one leg at a time.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          You climb onto the bed with your shoes on. A smear of garden dirt crosses the cover. You put your sleeve over it, then stop when something scrapes below the door.
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('kept-silence')>>The young voice begins a prayer behind the door. You hear "a child" and "both parents". A second voice interrupts, close enough to come from beneath your mattress. You pull your feet nearer.<<else>>Outside, a young voice is speaking too fast. You hear "a child" and "both parents". The other interrupts. A prayer follows, low enough that you cannot make out the words.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.known.auriga>>The prayer breaks around a name you heard much later. For a moment you see a black shape with branching antlers through the window. You blink and it is only the iron gate.<<elseif $LostLamb.known.bishop>>You hear a parent's plea in the pauses between the words. You put a hand over each ear, but the prayer keeps reaching you through your elbows.<<else>>The prayer stops. You lower one foot from the mattress, then hear the same words whispered from beneath it. You pull the foot back up.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          The loose stitch is beneath your finger. You hold it. <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('kept-silence')>>The young voice calls again, this time from the gap beneath the door.<<else>>A person below the window calls again, louder this time.<</if>>
        <<option 'CN'>>
          你又试了一次门闩，才把手指抽走。膝盖压过地毯的位置酸疼。你揉着一边，眼睛盯着门下的缝。
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('rest-space')>>你像在台阶上那样，先伸直一条腿，再扶床柱站起来。系得很难看的鞋带拖过地毯。你先避开它，才挪动另一只脚。<<else>>你站得太急，发麻的脚撑不住，折下去了。你重重坐回地上，捉住床柱，一条腿一条腿地站。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          你穿着鞋爬上床。花园里的泥在被子上蹭出一道印，你拿袖子盖住，门下传来刮擦，手便停了。
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('kept-silence')>>门后，年轻的声音开始祈祷。你听见“一个孩子”和“双亲”。第二个声音打断了他，近得像来自自己的床垫下面。你把双脚收得更近。<<else>>外面，年轻的声音说得很快。你听见“一个孩子”和“双亲”。另一个人打断了他。随后响起祈祷，低得听不清字。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.known.auriga>>祈祷在一个很久以后才听过的名字旁断开。窗外有一瞬间出现一道黑影，头上分岔的角向两边伸开。你眨眼，它又只是铁大门。<<elseif $LostLamb.known.bishop>>字与字之间，你听见父母的求饶。你用两只手捂耳朵，祈祷却还顺着胳膊传进来。<<else>>祈祷停了。你把一只脚放下床垫，下面便有人低声念出相同的话。你立刻将脚收回。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          松线就在手指下面。你勾住它。<<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('kept-silence')>>年轻的声音再次叫你，这次来自门下的缝。<<else>>窗下的人再次叫你，这次更响。<</if>>
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main-last-call'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('kept-silence')>>"Kylar?" The voice at the door has stopped pretending to be far away. You look through the window. Nobody is standing beneath it. "They won't come if you call now," it says. "You've kept them waiting too long."<<else>>"Kylar?" Someone calls from below the window. You push yourself up on one elbow. A second person tells them to keep away from the entrance. You hear a bag dropped, an angry reply, then the first voice again. "We can hear you. Keep talking."
          <br><br>
          You tell them which room. The answer comes back from below. Then the same answer comes from the door.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          The handle has not moved. Something is kneeling on the other side. Its voice is as close as a mouth pressed against the keyhole.
          <br><br>
          "They keep leaving you," it says. "The one with the pencils. The ones who put you to bed. The ones outside."
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('stay-vow-bound')>>It knocks twice, waits, and knocks again. You put your hand over your mouth. The voice repeats the promise you made about Sydney. "You already know how to keep someone."<<elseif $LostLamb.marks.includes('stay-vow-broken')>>It knocks twice, waits, and knocks again. There is a rip of paper under the last knock, exactly where you remember the drawing tearing. "You let one afternoon go. How many can you afford?"<<else>>It scratches once below the lock. The scratch reaches the floor on your side, though the door has not opened.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          "Give me your name. I'll keep everyone inside. You won't have to call again."
          <br><br>
          The bed gives a little beneath your hand. There is room beside you now. The pillow has another hollow, deep enough for a head, but no head is there. Downstairs, the scraping stops. Your parent's cup rings once against the table.
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.known.auriga>>For an instant, a voice you heard much later calls this a hole that needs filling. Another speaks of locks being gnawed open. You cannot hold either sentence. Your tongue is too small for the names in them.<<elseif $LostLamb.known.bishop>>There is a flash of red above an altar, then the cry of a parent begging for you. The closed door hides it at once. Something on the other side says, "They were allowed to keep you."<</if>>
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('kept-silence')>>A cart rattles past in the street. You lift your head to shout. The thing at the door says, "Promise first."<<else>>Outside, someone calls your name again. This time the thing at the door speaks over them. "Promise first."<</if>> The room is so quiet that you can hear the needle of the clock touch every mark.
        <<option 'CN'>>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('kept-silence')>>“凯拉尔？”门边的声音不再假装自己离得很远。你往窗外看，下面没有人。“现在喊，他们也不会来的。”它说，“你让他们等得太久了。”<<else>>“凯拉尔？”有人在窗下喊。你用一条胳膊撑起身子。另一个人让他别靠近入口。你听见袋子落地，一句生气的回答，然后又是先前的声音。“我们听得见。继续说话。”
          <br><br>
          你说出房间的位置。下面的人答应了。紧接着，门后也传来一模一样的回答。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          门把手没有动。有什么跪在另一侧，声音近得像嘴唇就贴着锁眼。
          <br><br>
          “他们总把你留下。”它说，“拿铅笔的那个。哄你上床的那些。外面的那些。”
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('stay-vow-bound')>>它敲两下，等一会儿，又敲一下。你用手捂住嘴。那个声音重复了你为悉尼作出的承诺。“你已经知道，怎样才能把人留住。”<<elseif $LostLamb.marks.includes('stay-vow-broken')>>它敲两下，等一会儿，又敲一下。最后一下下面夹着撕纸的声音，就在你记得画纸裂开的位置。“你已经放走了一个下午。还经得起几个？”<<else>>它在锁下刮了一下。门没有开，刮痕却一直伸到了你这边的地板上。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          “把你的名字给我。我会把所有人留在里面。以后就不用再喊了。”
          <br><br>
          手边的床垫轻轻陷下去。身旁现在空出一个位置，枕头上多了一处凹陷，深得够枕下一颗头，却没有头在那里。楼下的刮擦停了。父母的杯子在桌上轻响一声。
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.known.auriga>>一瞬间，有个很久以后才听过的声音，称这里是需要填补的洞。另一个说，有东西正啃开锁。你抓不住其中任何一句。舌头太小了，念不出里面那些名字。<<elseif $LostLamb.known.bishop>>祭坛上方闪过一片红，接着是父母为你求饶的哭声。紧闭的门立刻把它遮住。另一侧的东西说：“他们获准留下你了。”<</if>>
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('kept-silence')>>街上一辆车吱呀经过。你抬头想喊，门后的东西说：“先答应。”<<else>>外面又有人叫你的名字。这次，门后的东西抢在他前面开口。“先答应。”<</if>>屋里安静得，你能听见钟针碰到每一道刻度。
      <</language>>
    <<case 'main'>>
      <<language>>
        <<option 'EN'>>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-vow-offered')>>You say your name. The mouth at the keyhole finishes it before you do. The bed sinks beside you, and a small, cold hand settles over yours.
          <br><br>
          "Now don't wake them."
          <br><br>
          You turn towards the other pillow. Sydney's short pencil lies in its hollow. You pick it up, eager to show <<nnpc_him 'Sydney'>> that you kept it. The hand tightens. Beyond the door, two cups slide into place. You hear your parents' chairs drawn back, but nobody sits down.
          <br><br>
          The street goes quiet. Nobody calls from below the window. You try to call. Your mouth shapes the name you gave away and makes no sound. The hand turns your face back towards the empty pillow.
          <br><br>
          <span class="purple">Everyone is still inside.</span> You cannot find a voice among them. When you try to get out of bed, the small hand presses your wrist into the cover. The pencil rolls out of reach.
          <br><br>
          Somewhere far away, beside a different bed, another voice calls. It has to call again before you remember how to open your eyes.<<else>>"No." You say it against your own fingers. The door shudders hard enough to lift dust from the frame. The hollow in the pillow vanishes.
          <br><br>
          You shout towards the window. The first word catches in your throat. The second comes out too loud. <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('kept-silence')>>For a moment only the cart's wheels answer. You shout until your throat hurts. Someone in the street stops. "Who's up there?" They have not come from the temple. They cannot see you yet.<<else>>Below, someone answers at once. "There. That window." A latch rattles on the outside gate.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          Something silver strikes the bedroom door. You climb onto the pillow and shout again, giving them the room, the stairs, the place where they must not stand. The thing at the keyhole repeats each word a moment after you, but the voice outside keeps answering the first one.
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.known.bishop>>A parent's plea passes through the noise. For one breath you see red light on an altar and silver held above it. You stretch out a child's hand. There is only the bedroom door to touch.<<else>>You hear your parent behind the door, saying your name as they did when the button came loose. Before you can answer, a silver nail scrapes the wood beside your ear.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          The house has not mended. The hand under the other bed has not turned warm. <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('kept-silence')>>The stranger in the street asks whether the door is open. You cannot see whether they are coming nearer. You pull both feet onto the mattress and keep calling.<<else>>Somebody below asks for help, and another voice refuses to go farther without it. You pull both feet onto the mattress and keep calling.<</if>>
          <br><br>
          A voice beside another bed joins them. It uses a name that is yours now. You answer before the thing at the door can say it for you.<</if>>
        <<option 'CN'>>
          <<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('main-vow-offered')>>你说出自己的名字。锁眼旁的嘴抢在你前面念完。身旁的床垫沉下去，一只冰凉的小手覆在你的手上。
          <br><br>
          “现在，别吵醒他们。”
          <br><br>
          你转向另一只枕头。凹陷里躺着悉尼的短铅笔。你捡起来，急着让<<nnpc_him 'Sydney'>>看自己还留着它。那只手收紧。门外，两只杯子滑回原处。你听见父母的椅子被拉开，却没有人坐下。
          <br><br>
          街上安静了。窗下不再有人叫你。你试着喊，嘴唇摆出刚交出去的那个名字，却发不出声音。那只手将你的脸转回空枕头。
          <br><br>
          <span class="purple">所有人都还在屋里。</span>你却找不到其中任何一个的声音。你想下床，那只小手就把手腕压回被子上。铅笔滚到了够不着的地方。
          <br><br>
          很远的地方，另一张床旁有个声音在叫。它不得不再叫一遍，你才记起该怎样睁开眼睛。<<else>>“不。”你对着自己的手指说。门猛地震了一下，门框上的灰落下来。枕头上的凹陷消失了。
          <br><br>
          你朝窗户喊。第一个字卡在喉咙，第二个喊得太响。<<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('kept-silence')>>有那么一会儿，只有车轮回答。你一直喊到喉咙疼。街上有人停下来。“谁在上面？”他不是从神殿来的，还没有看见你。<<else>>下面立刻有人回答。“那里。那扇窗。”外面的大门闩响了。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          银色的东西撞上卧室门。你爬到枕头上，再喊一次，把房间、楼梯，还有不能站的位置都告诉他们。锁眼旁的东西慢一拍，重复你说的每一个字。外面的声音却一直回答先说出的那个。
          <br><br>
          <<if $LostLamb.known.bishop>>父母的一声求饶穿过那些响动。有一口气那么短，你看见祭坛上的红光，以及举在上面的银。你伸出孩子的手，能碰到的却只有卧室门。<<else>>门后传来父母的声音，像扣子掉下来时那样叫你的名字。你还没回答，一根银色指甲便擦过耳边的木头。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          房子没有修好，另一张床下的手也没有暖起来。<<if $LostLamb.marks.includes('kept-silence')>>街上的陌生人问门开着没有，你看不见他是否正在靠近。你把两只脚都收上床垫，继续喊。<<else>>下面有人去叫帮手，另一个说，人来之前不肯再往里走。你把两只脚都收上床垫，继续喊。<</if>>
          <br><br>
          另一张床旁的声音也加入了。它用的是如今属于你的名字。你抢在门后的东西替你念出来以前，答应了它。<</if>>
      <</language>>
  <</switch>>
<</widget>>
